you know what I mean?
你懂我意思吗？

157
00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.380
Like I had to have a little bit, like with the golf, I had to have a little bit of knack
就像我得有一点，就像打高尔夫一样，我得有一点打高尔夫的

158
00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:51.920
for golf.
天赋。

159
00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:52.460
Right.
没错。

160
00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.640
Like you have skill.
就像你得有技巧一样。

161
00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:54.620
Had to have a little skill.
得有一点技巧。

162
00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:54.900
Right.
没错。

163
00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.500
Director, I had to have some skill as a director.
导演，我作为导演也得有一些技巧。

164
00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.920
I had to know what I wanted to do.
我得知道自己想做什么。

165
00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.640
I had to have made some decisions, but then everybody else made it so easy, you know?
我得做出一些决定，但其他人让一切变得如此简单，你知道吗？

166
00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.780
So, it was a good time.
所以，那是一段美好的时光。

167
00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:10.060
Um, I loved everything about that answer, and now I want to pick up golf, so.
嗯，我喜欢这个回答的一切，现在我想去学打高尔夫了，所以。

168
00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:10.820
You do?
真的吗？

169
00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:11.640
Not really.
其实没有。

170
00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.300
Only at that course.
只在那座球场打。

171
00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.680
That course is pretty special.
那座球场相当特别。

172
00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:17.680
That course is pretty sweet.
那座球场相当棒。

173
00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.640
No, I can't mess up my tennis game, let's be real.
不，我不能搞砸我的网球水平，说实话。

174
00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.960
Yeah, stick with tennis, you know.
是啊，坚持打网球吧，你知道的。

175
00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.020
I just want you to make a golf movie now.
我现在就想让你拍一部高尔夫电影。

176
00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.680
I'm like, you should make a golf movie.
我在想，你应该拍一部高尔夫电影。

177
00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:26.740
Maybe that's my next movie.
也许那会是我的下一部电影。

178
00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:27.020
Yeah.
是啊。

179
00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:27.720
Maybe it should be.
也许应该拍一部。

180
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.240
Yeah, call it the caddy.
是啊，就叫《球童》吧。

181
00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.260
The caddy.
《球童》。

182
00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.400
So, Lee, I mean, you had been on the set many times.
那么，李，我是说，你以前多次去过片场。

183
00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.520
You had been around us shooting.
你曾待在我们拍摄的现场。

184
00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.700
You even had a role.
你甚至还演了一个角色。

185
00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:36.140
That's right.
没错。

186
00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.980
You were the lactation consultant.
你演的是哺乳顾问。

187
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:38.360
I was Clark.
我演的是克拉克。

188
00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:39.760
That's right.
没错。

189
00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:44.980
So, did you gain any new insights from being on the set from the perspective as a director?
那么，作为导演，在片场的经历让你获得了什么新的见解吗？

190
00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:46.400
That's a good question.
这是个好问题。

191
00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:51.660
You know, the thing is, okay, so I had directed indie films up to this point, right?
你知道，是这样的，好吧，在那之前我一直执导独立电影，对吧？

192
00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.520
So, an indie film, you're making the movie.
所以，拍独立电影时，你就是在制作电影。

193
00:06:54.860 --> 00:07:00.060
You guys know this, but for your listeners, you have 20 days or 21 days to shoot.
你们都知道，但对于听众来说，你只有20天或21天的时间来拍摄。

194
00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:01.020
110 pages.
110页的剧本。

195
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.980
You're moving really fast, you know.
你必须动作非常快，你知道的。

196
00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.720
And usually the first time it's kind of messy.
而且通常第一次拍的时候会有点乱。

197
00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.680
And then you start the job of the director is to kind of shape it, you know.
然后你开始工作，导演的工作就是去塑造它，你知道。

198
00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.720
Like, maybe don't take your jacket off.
比如，也许别脱掉你的夹克。

199
00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.980
And maybe take a breath before you stand up to go, you know.
也许在起身离开前先深呼吸一下，你知道。

200
00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.940
And slowly you kind of form this scene, you know.
然后慢慢地你就能塑造出这场戏，你知道。

201
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.460
But at the same time, you're rushing too, you know.
但与此同时，你也在赶时间，你知道的。

202
00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.540
You're like holding your breath.
你就像屏住了呼吸一样。

203
00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:21.780
So, take that.
所以，接受这一点吧。

204
00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.720
And then I walk on the office, right?
然后我走进办公室，对吧？

205
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.760
And so, here's the experience.
所以，这就是当时的体验。

206
00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.200
We would set up a shot, you know.
我们会布置一个镜头，你知道的。

207
00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:33.240
And I'd kind of tell Matt Sohn, who was the DP, who was just an incredible person to work with.
我会告诉摄影指导Matt Sohn，他是一个非常棒的合作对象。

208
00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.840
I'd say, you know, I want to have maybe they come in over here.
我会说，你知道，我想让他们从这边进来。

209
00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.440
And we play this scene at the reception.
然后我们在接待处演这场戏。

210
00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.080
And, you know, he's like, great.
然后，你知道，他会说，太棒了。

211
00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:39.860
We light the scene.
我们布置好灯光。

212
00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.020
You guys come on set.
你们来到片场。

213
00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.480
And it's like, you guys are walking on with like a cup of coffee.
就像是，你们拿着咖啡走进来。

214
00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.460
And you're like, what are we seeing?
然后你们会问，我们这是在看什么？

215
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:45.900
Are we doing?
我们在做什么？

216
00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:46.240
You know.
你知道的。

217
00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:02.320
By season nine, we would just truly, we would like, be like, what are we doing right now?
到了第九季，我们真的会经常问，我们现在到底在干什么？

218
00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:02.740
Yeah.
是啊。

219
00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.040
Like, sitting down, wondering, what is the scene?
就像坐下来，纳闷，这场戏到底是什么？

220
00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:07.880
Especially if we didn't have huge chunks of dialogue.
尤其是当我们没有大段台词的时候。

221
00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:14.100
If you're just going to like cruise through reception and Angela goes, excuse me, is that, like, and that's all I say?
如果你只是要穿过接待处，然后Angela说，打扰一下，是那个吗，就像这样，而我只说了这些？

222
00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.400
Yeah, not a lot of preparation.
是啊，没多少准备工作。

223
00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:19.140
I'm going to wait and just like, like, figure it out on set.
我打算等着，然后在片场临时发挥。

224
00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.320
But the funny thing is, so that's what happens.
但有趣的是，事情就是这样发生的。

225
00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.320
And then everybody in their play, I tell you guys, oh, you're going to come in here, do this scene here, the reception, blah, blah, blah.
然后每个人各就各位，我告诉你们，哦，你们要从这儿进来，在这儿演这场戏，在接待处，巴拉巴拉之类的。

226
00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:28.660
Okay, let's try one.
好了，试拍一次。

227
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.200
Action.
开始。

228
00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:32.860
And then a perfectly executed scene happens.
然后一场完美执行的戏就诞生了。

229
00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:33.920
Like, everything.
真的，一切都恰到好处。

230
00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.600
Like, every moment's perfect.
每一个瞬间都很完美。

231
00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.540
Every joke's perfect.
每一个笑点都很完美。

232
00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:37.420
Every nuance's perfect.
每一个细微之处都很完美。

233
00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:38.940
Okay, cut.
好了，停。

234
00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:42.640
Everybody looks at me and it's like, I got to have something to say.
每个人都看着我，好像我得说点什么似的。

235
00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:43.200
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

236
00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.600
Besides just, we could move on.
除了说，我们可以继续下一场了。

237
00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:46.160
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

238
00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.080
So, that was a challenge.
所以，那是一个挑战。

239
00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:50.960
Like, that was a challenge to find.
那是一个需要去应对的挑战。

240
00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:55.620
Of course, there was a number of spots where, like, I had to actually do some directing.
当然，也有一些地方我确实需要进行一些导演工作。

241
00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:56.720
But a lot of it was that.
但大部分情况就是那样。

242
00:08:56.860 --> 00:09:03.920
A lot of it, my job was having a vision for how the scene should work and then just kind of keeping everybody's spirits up.
我的工作很大程度上是对场景如何运作有一个构想，然后保持大家的士气。

243
00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.400
Being in a good mood, keeping everybody loose, you know, and trying different takes and trying to have fun.
保持好心情，让大家放松，你知道，尝试不同的拍摄方式，尽量玩得开心。

244
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:18.340
But it was so much different than doing an indie film where you're just constantly, you're looking at your watch, you know, and you're stressing and you're just trying to get,
但这和拍独立电影太不一样了，拍独立电影时你总是看着手表，你知道，你会感到压力，只是想尽力去……

245
00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:18.800
you know, shape.
你知道，成型。

246
00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.120
Just a hustle, hustle, hustle.
就是不停地忙碌、忙碌、忙碌。

247
00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:22.400
Yeah, and you're worried that you're not going to get it, you know?
是啊，而且你担心拍不到想要的镜头，你知道吗？

248
00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.940
There was no worry we weren't going to get it.
我们完全不用担心拍不到。

249
00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.780
We got it on take one every time, I felt like.
我觉得我们每次都是一条过。

250
00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:32.320
Well, Lee, I remember you telling me that you did have a few ideas that you wanted to throw in there that you talked to Matt Soane about.
嗯，Lee，我记得你告诉过我，你确实有一些想加入的想法，还和Matt Sohn讨论过。

251
00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:33.100
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

252
00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.000
And he kind of had to let you down gently.
他当时不得不委婉地拒绝你。

253
00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.480
Well, he was awesome.
嗯，他真的很棒。

254
00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:44.080
So when we first walked through, so you get your script and then, like, a week before your shooting,
所以当我们第一次走场时，你会拿到剧本，然后大概在开拍前一周，

255
00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:50.280
the DP and the director are going to walk through the set and kind of look at and kind of form an idea of what the shoot's going to be like.
摄影指导和导演会去现场走一遍，构思一下拍摄会是什么样子。

256
00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:59.040
And so I said to Matt, I had this idea because I always loved on those old episodes, especially on the British office, but they did it, I think I did it on American too,
所以我跟马特提过，我有个想法，因为我一直很喜欢那些老剧集里的镜头，特别是英版《办公室》，我想美版里我也做过，

257
00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:07.320
where just in a transition that you just cut to a copy machine, just making copies or, like, just someone, like, walking across, like,
就是在转场时切到一个复印机正在复印，或者有人走过，比如，

258
00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:08.940
delivering a piece of paper to someone's desk.
给某人的桌上送一份文件。

259
00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:14.180
Just that little quiet shot that, like, reminds you this is a documentary, right?
就是那种安静的小镜头，提醒观众这是一部纪录片，对吧？

260
00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:20.060
So I thought, I'd be fun to put one of those in, you know, that would be my little Easter egg that I'm going to put in this episode.
所以我心想，加一个这样的镜头会很有趣，你知道，那会是我在这集里埋的一个小彩蛋。

261
00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:23.120
So I said to Matt, I'd love to do one of these, like, little shots.
所以我跟马特说，我很想拍这种小镜头。

262
00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:29.880
And he said, well, we can shoot whatever you want, but I can promise you that won't go in the episode.
他说，你想拍什么都可以，但我敢保证那段不会出现在正片里。

263
00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.680
Because he was like – and he was right.
因为他觉得——而且他是对的。

264
00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.520
I mean, there was no time for it.
我是说，根本没时间拍那个。

265
00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:43.200
And at the end of the day, you know, Claire and I, who was the editor, we were doing everything we could to keep every piece of that episode in there.
说到底，我和剪辑师克莱尔当时竭尽全力想保留这一集的每一个片段。

266
00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.460
And, of course, that was impossible.
当然，那是不可能的。

267
00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:45.760
And there's a whole storyline.
还有整整一条故事线。

268
00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:52.280
There's a whole – not a storyline, but there's a whole sequence that was cut, which was – I don't know if you remember, we did a whole driving sequence.
有一整段——不算故事线，但有一整段戏被剪掉了，就是——我不记得你还记不记得，我们拍了一整段开车戏。

269
00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:52.820
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

270
00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:53.100
I do.
我记得。

271
00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.220
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

272
00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:55.120
Is it in deleted scenes?
在删减片段里吗？

273
00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:55.900
Okay, yeah.
好的，没错。

274
00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.680
And there's a whole runner with Toby that's hilarious in deleted scenes.
还有一段关于托比的戏，在删减片段里特别搞笑。

275
00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:00.160
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

276
00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.620
That I want to share when we get to it.
等我们聊到那儿的时候我想分享一下。

277
00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:07.100
But it's – he's trying to impress Nellie when he questions Frank.
就是他试图在审问弗兰克时给内莉留下好印象。

278
00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.200
Yes, of course.
对，当然。

279
00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.140
I remember that.
我记得那个。

280
00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:10.920
I remember that.
我记得那个。

281
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:11.140
Yeah.
没错。

282
00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:13.640
So that was fun, though.
不过那段确实很有趣。

283
00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.080
Well, I absolutely loved episodes where Pam and Dwight got to team up.
我特别喜欢帕姆和德怀特联手的那些集数。

284
00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:28.560
And on this episode, I remember in the crafting of it, because I was in the writer's room, I was saying, could we please have a scene where Pam and Dwight have, like, a stakeout?
在这一集里，我记得在创作阶段，因为我当时在编剧室，我就提议，能不能加一场戏，让帕姆和德怀特一起蹲点？

285
00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:32.580
I wanted them – I don't know, Angela, if this is part of early mom.
我当时想让他们——安吉拉，我不知道这算不算“早期妈妈”的一部分。

286
00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:33.700
Yeah, it is.
对，算。

287
00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:37.760
I wanted to have this moment where they were spying on everybody in the warehouse.
我想让他们有一个监视仓库里所有人的时刻。

288
00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:41.780
And I just remember we had so much fun doing all those scenes, all the Pam and Dwight scenes.
我只记得我们拍那些戏的时候特别开心，所有帕姆和德怀特的戏份。

289
00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.080
Yeah, those were a lot of fun.
没错，那些确实很有趣。

290
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:51.720
And you guys is just – your chemistry and your – you know, the Pam and Dwight, like, seeing those two team up was just a lot of fun.
你们俩的化学反应，还有你们——你知道，帕姆和德怀特，看到他们俩联手真的太有意思了。

291
00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:51.960
Yeah.
没错。

292
00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.320
And there was a lot of fun stuff.
当时有很多好玩的东西。

293
00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.340
I remember – the one thing I remember about that was, in terms of directing,
我记得——关于那场戏，从导演的角度来看，我记得的一件事是，

294
00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:05.480
was before the scene – there's a scene where you guys are spying on the warehouse and Dwight has a pair of binoculars he's looking through.
在拍摄之前——有一场戏是你们在监视仓库，德怀特拿着一副望远镜在看。

295
00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:05.860
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

296
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.740
So, moments before, Phil Shea, the prop guy.
就在那之前，道具师菲尔·谢。

297
00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:08.980
Yeah.
没错。

298
00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:09.240
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

299
00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.720
He comes up to me and he shows me two different binoculars.
他走过来给我看两副不同的望远镜。

300
00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.840
It's the – you know, which ones would Dwight be using, right?
就是——你知道，问我德怀特会用哪一副，对吧？

301
00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:16.080
Sure.
当然。

302
00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:16.420
This is very Phil.
这很菲尔。

303
00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:22.680
One was very small, very small, tiny binoculars, and one was very big, okay?
一副非常小，非常小，微型的望远镜，另一副非常大，好吗？

304
00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:25.800
And I'm thinking, oh, man, this is a real test, you know?
我在想，天哪，这真是个考验，你知道吗？

305
00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:26.900
This is a real teSt.
这真是个考验。

306
00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:30.740
I thought the small ones would be funny because I thought it would be funny.
我以为小的会很有趣，因为我觉得那样会很滑稽。

307
00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.740
Like, he whips something out and then it's, like, ridiculously small.
就像他突然掏出什么东西，结果却小得离谱。

308
00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:34.140
Yeah.
是啊。

309
00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.380
So, I said, oh, these.
所以我说，哦，就这些。

310
00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:37.220
So, Rain walks on set.
然后，雷恩走进片场。

311
00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:39.980
He looks at the binoculars.
他看了看望远镜。

312
00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:42.380
He goes, is there another set of binoculars?
他说，还有另一副望远镜吗？

313
00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.060
And Phil goes, I got these big ones.
菲尔就说，我还有这些大的。

314
00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.200
He's like, yeah, I want the big ones.
他就像是，好，我就要大的那副。

315
00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:48.140
So, I failed that teSt.
所以，我没通过那个考验。

316
00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:48.880
Oh, no.
哦，不。

317
00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.820
Well, you should know.
好吧，你应该知道的。

318
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:56.740
I nicknamed Rain on set Carrot Top because he loved a trunk full of props.
我在片场给雷恩起了个绰号叫“胡萝卜顶”，因为他特别喜欢带一后备箱的道具。

319
00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.540
I was like, the man loved a lot of props.
我当时就想，这家伙真是太爱道具了。

320
00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:02.700
It's no surprise to me that he wanted the big, over-the-top binoculars.
他想要那副夸张的大望远镜，我一点也不觉得奇怪。

321
00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:03.240
Amazing.
太棒了。

322
00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:03.680
Amazing.
太棒了。

323
00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.560
It made sense, too.
这也说得通。

324
00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.060
When we shot it, I was like, oh, yeah, okay, I see the big ones.
我们拍摄的时候，我心想，哦，对，好吧，我明白为什么要用大的了。

325
00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:07.700
That's funny.
那很有趣。

326
00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:08.360
All right.
好吧。

327
00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:14.240
Well, Jenna and I weren't there when you shot all of those scenes with Craig and John as horrible roommates.
珍娜和我当时不在场，没能看到你们和克雷格、约翰拍那些糟糕室友的戏份。

328
00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:18.100
Like, Jim and Daryl were such bad roommates, but Jim is such a slob.
吉姆和达里尔真是糟糕的室友，但吉姆实在太邋遢了。

329
00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.280
I just loved all of these scenes.
我非常喜欢所有这些场景。

330
00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.700
I loved thinking about how two people lived together on the show.
我喜欢去想剧中的两个人是怎么住在一起的。

331
00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.840
We never got to see that.
我们从来没机会看到。

332
00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:28.340
We never even go into Pam and Jim's home and see how they lived together.
我们甚至都没进过帕姆和吉姆的家，看看他们是怎么住在一起的。

333
00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:28.640
True.
确实。

334
00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:35.420
We saw a snippet of how Dwight and Moe's lived together, but I loved seeing Jim and Daryl.
我们看过一点德怀特和莫斯住在一起的样子，但我很喜欢看吉姆和达里尔的戏。

335
00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.960
And can you tell us about shooting those apartment scenes?
你能跟我们讲讲拍摄那些公寓场景的事吗？

336
00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:42.580
Man, shooting with John and Craig, we had such a blaSt.
天哪，和约翰、克雷格一起拍戏，我们玩得太开心了。

337
00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:42.920
I bet.
我敢肯定。

338
00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.760
We had so much fun.
我们玩得特别尽兴。

339
00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.200
We couldn't get through takes.
我们总是拍不下去。

340
00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:49.920
You know, we were just laughing and goofing off and having so much fun.
你知道，我们一直在笑，一直在胡闹，玩得特别开心。

341
00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:59.780
And I remember the first scene we shot in that apartment was when Daryl comes back on his lunch break and Jim is sitting there and Daryl's got that little cooler.
我记得我们在那间公寓拍的第一场戏，是达里尔午休回来，吉姆坐在那儿，达里尔提着那个小冷藏箱。

342
00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:00.300
Yeah.
是啊。

343
00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:01.440
He opens it up.
他把它打开了。

344
00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.260
He opens it up.
他把它打开了。

345
00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.060
And there was something about that cooler, man.
那个冷藏箱真是有什么魔力，伙计。

346
00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:07.820
Something about the way he was holding that thing that we couldn't get through it.
他拿那个东西的方式，让我们总是拍不下去。

347
00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:08.980
I mean, they couldn't get through it.
我是说，他们总是拍不下去。

348
00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:10.540
They were laughing so hard.
他们笑得太厉害了。

349
00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:12.380
And I would be like, okay, cut.
我只好说，好了，卡。

350
00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:12.920
We'll try it again.
我们再来一次。

351
00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.080
And it wasn't working.
而且根本没用。

352
00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.780
So finally, I just let them go.
所以最后，我干脆随他们去了。

353
00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:16.300
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

354
00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:16.560
Yeah.
嗯。

355
00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:19.920
Let them just laugh and laugh and laugh and kind of laugh it out of themselves.
就让他们笑个够，笑个不停，直到把那股劲儿笑完。

356
00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:22.440
But, man, that was so fun.
但是，天哪，那真的太好玩了。

357
00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:23.960
Like, that was just a total blaSt.
简直是太棒了。

358
00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.720
And those guys were so fun together.
而且他们在一起真的很有趣。

359
00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:27.960
Like, they were really working off each other.
他们之间的互动真的很有火花。

360
00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.680
Same with you and Rain, Jenna.
你和雷恩也是，珍娜。

361
00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:33.740
Like, you guys were just like such a fun chemistry going on there.
你们俩之间也有那种非常有趣的化学反应。

362
00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:37.460
Well, I remember you coming home from that shoot day.
嗯，我记得你那天拍完戏回家。

363
00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:42.380
And it was very clear to me that you had just spent the entire day bro-ing out with those guys.
很明显，你那天整天都在和那帮家伙称兄道弟。

364
00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.260
You were like, they're so funny.
你说他们太搞笑了。

365
00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:47.720
We just kept laughing.
我们一直在笑。

366
00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:53.940
But then also, I remember you coming home from when you shot at the senator's house with Angela Bryan and Oscar.
但我也记得你拍完在参议员家那场戏回家时，和安吉拉、布莱恩还有奥斯卡一起拍的那次。

367
00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:55.960
And you had a lot of fun at that, too.
你在那次拍摄中也玩得很开心。

368
00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:01.600
But I remember you told me a story from that one where you said was one of the most challenging moments of the shoot, which took me by surprise.
但我记得你跟我讲过那次拍摄的一个故事，你说那是拍摄中最具挑战性的时刻之一，这让我很惊讶。

369
00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.300
Well, yeah, you're talking about the baby.
嗯，对，你说的是那个婴儿。

370
00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:05.760
The baby.
那个婴儿。

371
00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:11.520
Right, okay, so this is actually, this is a good example of more independent filmmaking, right?
没错，好吧，这其实是一个很好的独立电影制作的例子，对吧？

372
00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:12.540
Because we weren't on the set.
因为我们当时不在摄影棚。

373
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.580
We were in a house.
我们在一个房子里。

374
00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:19.480
So, like, when you're shooting on the set, it was kind of obvious how scenes would be blocked out because everyone kind of had their spot.
所以，在摄影棚拍摄时，场景调度是很明显的，因为每个人都有自己的位置。

375
00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:23.820
So, if it was Angela's scene, you knew you'd probably be over in accounting and that's how you're going to, you know.
所以，如果是安吉拉的戏，你就知道你大概会在会计部那边，这就是你要待的地方。

376
00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.800
But shooting in a house, it's like no one's ever been here before.
但在房子里拍摄，就像是大家都没来过这里一样。

377
00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:27.360
Right.
没错。

378
00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:28.700
And we had a ton of extras.
而且我们有很多群演。

379
00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:33.680
So, there was this element of, like, okay, I really have to direct this stuff.
所以，有一种感觉就是，好吧，我真的得亲自执导这些东西。

380
00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:40.180
So, that scene with the baby in the little white communion outfit, I remember, like, staging that.
所以，那场婴儿穿着白色圣餐服的戏，我记得当时在排练。

381
00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.300
And I thought, okay, we'll put it in the living room.
我想，好吧，我们把它放在客厅里。

382
00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:48.800
And then you guys would kind of appear as if you're kind of almost presenting yourself, standing up a little higher than everybody and have this moment.
然后你们会像是在展示自己一样出现，站得比别人稍微高一点，然后完成那个瞬间。

383
00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.500
And so, let's try it.
所以，我们试了一下。

384
00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:53.040
So, we did it and it worked.
我们拍了，效果不错。

385
00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:53.660
It was fine.
挺好的。

386
00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:54.220
It was good.
很棒。

387
00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:56.420
I was like, great, let's do another one.
我当时想，太好了，再来一条。

388
00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:01.100
And around that time, that baby decided, I'm not doing another one of these things.
就在那时，那个婴儿决定，我才不要再拍一遍呢。

389
00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:05.480
And started squirming at first and then just crying and having a fit.
起初开始扭动，然后就开始大哭大闹。

390
00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.480
And I was like, oh, no, no.
我当时想，噢，不，不。

391
00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:08.660
Like, let's try it.
再试一次吧。

392
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:09.940
Can we fix this?
我们能解决吗？

393
00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.420
You know, is there another baby?
你知道，还有别的婴儿吗？

394
00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:12.000
What are we going to do?
我们该怎么办？

395
00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.240
And there wasn't another baby and we couldn't fix it.
但没有别的婴儿了，我们也解决不了。

396
00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:20.960
But then Rusty, who was, you know, you guys know Rusty, the first AD, he said to me, you know, we got one take.
但后来拉斯蒂，你们知道拉斯蒂，我们的第一副导演，他跟我说，我们只有一条素材可用。

397
00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:24.680
And I was like, yeah, but is that good?
我当时说，是啊，但那条好吗？

398
00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:25.620
He's like, I think it was pretty good.
他说，我觉得挺好的。

399
00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.880
Anyway, that is the take that's in the show.
总之，最终用在剧里的就是那一条。

400
00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:28.280
The first take.
第一条。

401
00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:28.980
The only one.
唯一的那个。

402
00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.040
That was the only one we got.
那是我们拍到的唯一一个。

403
00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:30.480
Yeah.
是啊。

404
00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:43.000
I remember breaking quite a bit when we took the group photo because I was looking back and none of our dialogue, me and Oscar's dialogue, is scripted.
我记得拍合照的时候我笑场了好几次，因为我回头看的时候，我和奥斯卡的对话完全没有剧本。

405
00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.120
I didn't think so.
我没觉得。

406
00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.780
I had a suspicion.
我当时就怀疑过。

407
00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.220
It's not scripted.
那不是剧本写的。

408
00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.560
And so literally what the script says is that Angela elbows Oscar.
剧本上写的其实就是安吉拉用手肘撞了奥斯卡一下。

409
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:53.800
Oscar says out.
奥斯卡说“出去”。

410
00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:54.660
That's it.
就这些。

411
00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:55.460
That's it.
就这些。

412
00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.440
So everything else you see is us.
所以你们看到的其他内容都是我们自己发挥的。

413
00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.600
And I when I watched it, I see myself breaking.
我回看的时候，看到自己笑场了。

414
00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:00.480
I like look down.
我低下了头。

415
00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.500
I'm like, because that was amazing.
我当时想，因为那太精彩了。

416
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.260
Yeah, that was really fun.
是啊，那真的很有趣。

417
00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:05.100
That was really funny.
真的很好笑。

418
00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:05.600
Yeah.
是啊。

419
00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:06.680
I'm surprised we got through that.
我很惊讶我们竟然拍完了。

420
00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:07.340
I know.
我知道。

421
00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:07.900
Me too.
我也是。

422
00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:14.960
Well, speaking of being surprised we got through things, I know that there were two other scenes that were very challenging to shoot.
说到惊讶我们能拍完，我知道还有另外两场戏拍起来非常有挑战性。

423
00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:15.560
Yeah.
是啊。

424
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.000
Do you want to share?
你想分享一下吗？

425
00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:20.520
Well, we had the Brian character and he had a couple of big moments.
嗯，我们有布莱恩这个角色，他有几个重头戏。

426
00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.200
So we had the fight, for example.
比如那场打斗戏。

427
00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:22.680
Yeah.
是啊。

428
00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.940
You know, that took some choreography to figure out.
你知道，那需要编排动作才能搞定。

429
00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:30.240
And we had, you know, and we had that actor, Brad, who played Frank, who was, you know, such a big imposing figure.
而且我们还有那个演员，布拉德，他饰演弗兰克，他是一个身材魁梧、很有压迫感的人。

430
00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.500
So to try to figure that out was a little bit of a challenge.
所以要处理好那场戏有点挑战性。

431
00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.600
And also, Brian had that equipment.
而且，布莱恩当时还拿着设备。

432
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:35.620
Oh, he had the boom.
哦，他拿着吊杆麦克风。

433
00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:36.500
He had the boom and stuff.
他拿着吊杆麦克风之类的东西。

434
00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:36.680
Yeah.
是啊。

435
00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.180
He couldn't just throw it on the ground.
他不能直接把它扔在地上。

436
00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.400
Like, he had to kind of, like, gently set it down.
他得把它轻轻地放下。

437
00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:41.940
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

438
00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.800
I remember that whole conversation.
我记得整个对话过程。

439
00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:44.220
And then fight.
然后才是打斗。

440
00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:44.450
Yes.
没错。

441
00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:47.760
So there was this weird moment of, like, he had to, like, gently put his stuff down.
所以当时有个很奇怪的瞬间，就是他得先把东西轻轻放下。

442
00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.180
So that was a little tricky.
所以那有点棘手。

443
00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:56.180
But the trickiest scene was definitely the reveal of you guys in that closet.
但最棘手的绝对是你们在那个储物间被发现的那场戏。

444
00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:56.920
Yes.
没错。

445
00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:57.240
Right?
对吧？

446
00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:57.600
Yes.
是的。

447
00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:06.020
And so, and in the script, I don't remember exactly how it was worded, but somehow it alluded to, like, we have a scene in the closet, and then you guys leave the closet,
剧本里，我不记得具体是怎么写的了，但大概暗示了我们有一场在储物间的戏，然后你们离开储物间，

448
00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:09.020
and we realize the closet is, like, right in the wall.
然后我们意识到储物间就在墙里。

449
00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:09.940
It was the opposite.
正好相反。

450
00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:11.620
I went back, and I read the script.
我回去读了剧本。

451
00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:16.200
It was that we're walking through somewhere.
当时我们正走在某个地方。

452
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:24.500
It described it as, like, a hallway into this little room, and then at the end, we walk out.
剧本描述的是，就像一条通往小房间的走廊，然后走到尽头，我们走出来。

453
00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:25.520
Kind of what you're saying.
和你说的差不多。

454
00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:29.080
At the end, we were to walk out and reveal that it was the closet.
最后，我们要走出来，揭示那其实是个储藏室。

455
00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:29.640
That's right.
没错。

456
00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:30.000
Yes.
是的。

457
00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:30.660
Yeah, yeah.
对，没错。

458
00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:41.660
But I remember doing that scene, Lee, and the whole conversation with Brian, doing it, like, on the move, like, walking and talking, and me saying, I'm really sorry.
但我记得拍那场戏的时候，李，我和布莱恩的整段对话都是在移动中完成的，边走边说，我说，我真的很抱歉。

459
00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:43.500
They shouldn't have fired you.
他们本不该解雇你的。

460
00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.820
It was like you couldn't get any tension.
感觉就像你无法营造出任何紧张感。

461
00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:51.520
You couldn't get any of the emotion of the scene by doing it as a walk and talk.
通过边走边说的方式，你无法传达出那场戏的任何情感。

462
00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:51.800
Yeah.
是啊。

463
00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:55.400
And then getting in and out of there, it just was very awkward.
而且进进出出的，感觉非常尴尬。

464
00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:56.060
Yeah.
是啊。

465
00:18:56.340 --> 00:19:00.020
And we spent, oh, my God, I don't even know how much time trying to figure that out.
我们花了，天哪，我甚至不知道花了多少时间去琢磨那个场景。

466
00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:00.840
Trying to figure it out.
一直在想办法解决。

467
00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:10.040
And it was Owen, the writer, Owen, who had the brilliant idea of how we ended up shooting it, which is that we shot it sort of as a spy shot.
是编剧欧文，欧文想出了一个绝妙的主意，也就是我们最终拍摄的方式，我们把它拍得像偷拍一样。

468
00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.960
And we pushed in so that you couldn't tell where we were as a viewer.
我们推进镜头，这样观众就看不出我们在哪里。

469
00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:16.200
You would just see where.
你只会看到我们在哪里。

470
00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:21.260
And then as you left, we pulled back and revealed where this closet was.
然后当你离开时，我们拉回镜头，揭示了那个储藏室的位置。

471
00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:25.060
I loved that because, of course, that door has been a mystery for us.
我喜欢那个设计，因为那扇门对我们来说一直是个谜。

472
00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:27.000
You know, everyone's like, what's behind that door?
你知道，每个人都在问，那扇门后面是什么？

473
00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:32.740
But, you know, it's also the door where Jim and Pam hook up where they made Philip.
但你知道，那也是吉姆和帕姆幽会的地方，他们就是在那里怀上菲利普的。

474
00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:33.500
Yes.
没错。

475
00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:38.300
And then also it's the door where we wanted to escape during the fire drill, which does not make sense.
而且那也是我们在消防演习时想要逃进去的门，虽然这根本说不通。

476
00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:38.700
Yes.
是的。

477
00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.760
Because we got some fan mail about that, actually.
因为我们确实收到了一些关于此的粉丝来信。

478
00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:46.640
People noted, why would they be trying to run into a closet during this fire?
人们指出，为什么他们在火灾时要往储藏室里跑？

479
00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:47.300
Yeah.
是啊。

480
00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:48.960
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

481
00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:50.300
Yeah,
是啊，

482
00:19:50.520 --> 00:20:01.140
so when we sat down kind of over the summer and the beginning of the year with the writers to talk about what things do we want to tie up and what things do we want to reveal in this final season,
所以当我们在夏天和年初与编剧们坐下来讨论，在这一最终季里我们想交代哪些事情，想揭示哪些秘密时，

483
00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:03.500
I can't remember who pitched it.
我不记得是谁提出来的了。

484
00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:08.000
I wish I did, but someone said we should finally find out what's behind that dang door.
我真希望我记得，但有人说我们终于应该揭开那扇该死的门后面到底是什么了。

485
00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:09.300
I love that.
我喜欢这个主意。

486
00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.020
That's amazing.
太棒了。

487
00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.620
Yeah, so we let you know.
是啊，所以我们让你知道了。

488
00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:12.880
And you were there.
而且你当时也在场。

489
00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:13.520
I was there.
我在场。

490
00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:14.780
The big door reveal.
大揭秘时刻。

491
00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.100
You made it happen.
是你促成了这一切。

492
00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.380
I did the door reveal.
我完成了这个揭秘。

493
00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:16.980
Yeah.
没错。

494
00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:22.560
Well, Leigh, before we wrap up our interview, Josh made lemon Madelines for us.
好了，利，在结束采访之前，乔什为我们做了柠檬玛德琳蛋糕。

495
00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.440
Oh, Josh.
噢，乔什。

496
00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:24.020
Hey.
嘿。

497
00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:25.840
Josh, you're such a good baker.
乔什，你真是个出色的烘焙师。

498
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.580
And I can't not bring them out.
我不能不把它们拿出来。

499
00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.320
So there you go.
给你。

500
00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:30.020
Everyone gets lemon Madelines today.
今天每个人都有柠檬玛德琳蛋糕吃。

501
00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.000
This is nice.
这真不错。

502
00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:32.660
This is now both our husbands are here.
现在我们的丈夫都在这儿了。

503
00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:33.380
Thank you, Josh.
谢谢你，乔什。

504
00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:33.480
They are.
确实是。

505
00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.100
Thank you, Josh.
谢谢你，乔什。

506
00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:37.560
Josh threw his Madelines and Leigh literally here.
乔什把他的玛德琳蛋糕和莉直接扔在这儿了。

507
00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:38.160
Literally sitting here.
就坐在那儿。

508
00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:39.980
Eating a Madeline.
吃着玛德琳蛋糕。

509
00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.200
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

510
00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:46.860
Well, Leigh, to wrap things up before you go, how did you like directing television versus movies?
好吧，莉，在你离开前总结一下，你觉得执导电视剧和电影有什么不同？

511
00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:49.820
You have not directed any more television since.
从那以后你就没再执导过电视剧了。

512
00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:51.140
Is that because you hated it?
是因为你讨厌执导电视剧吗？

513
00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:51.500
No.
不是。

514
00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:54.340
Well, actually, actually, I loved it.
其实，说实话，我挺喜欢的。

515
00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.900
Well, I don't know if you remember what happened, but.
嗯，我不知道你还记不记得当时发生了什么，但是……

516
00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:57.200
Yeah.
嗯。

517
00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:01.180
So I directed this episode and I loved it.
我执导了那一集，我很喜欢。

518
00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:01.580
I loved it.
我真的很喜欢。

519
00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:02.280
It was so fun.
太有趣了。

520
00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.860
And I thought, oh, I want to maybe do some more of this.
当时我想，噢，或许我想多做点这个。

521
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:09.220
Maybe you don't want to be attached to your stressful watch doing the independent filMs.
也许你不想再被独立电影那种压力大的工作束缚了。

522
00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:12.560
I want to do more of these where you just kind of keep it on the rails.
我想多做点这种只要按部就班就能完成的工作。

523
00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:12.840
Yeah.
是啊。

524
00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:17.960
And so I remember I had some meetings about maybe doing New Girl, maybe doing Brooklyn Nine-Nine,
所以我记得我开过几次会，谈论过或许可以执导《杰茜驾到》或者《神烦警探》，

525
00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.260
but they weren't shooting then.
但当时它们还没开拍。

526
00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.380
And so that was on the horizon.
所以那还在计划之中。

527
00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.400
But then I went off and made a film.
但后来我离开去拍了一部电影。

528
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.820
And then after I made the film, we moved to London.
拍完电影后，我们就搬到了伦敦。

529
00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:27.460
Remember?
还记得吗？

530
00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:31.380
Yes, I did a series there and you edited the film in London.
记得，我在那儿拍了一部剧，而你在伦敦剪辑那部电影。

531
00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:31.860
In London.
在伦敦。

532
00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:36.740
So by the time I finally came back to L.A., it was like a year later, you know, and the
所以等我终于回到洛杉矶时，已经是一年以后了，你知道，

533
00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:38.220
office wasn't on the air anymore.
《办公室》已经停播了。

534
00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:40.380
And that's crazy.
那太疯狂了。

535
00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:43.280
Those execs weren't at Fox anymore.
那些高管也不在福克斯工作了。

536
00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.820
And I kind of missed my moment.
我错过了我的时机。

537
00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:46.740
Like, it's hard.
这很难。

538
00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.980
It's a very hard job to get, like a TV director.
想要成为一名电视剧导演是一份非常难得的工作。

539
00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:49.180
Yeah.
是啊。

540
00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:51.400
Just job just to be that TV director.
仅仅是作为一名电视剧导演这份工作本身就很难。

541
00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.900
And so I kind of missed my moment.
所以我错过了我的时机。

542
00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:55.400
And it's a regret, you know, it's a regret.
这是一种遗憾，你知道，这是一种遗憾。

543
00:21:55.600 --> 00:22:01.460
So I guess if anyone out there, if you got Ron Howard tapped up and he can't do it, you
所以我想，如果外面有谁，如果你已经联系了朗·霍华德但他没空，

544
00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:02.120
know who to call.
你知道该找谁。

545
00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:03.140
We sure do.
我们当然知道。

546
00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:04.860
Well, let me tell you something.
好吧，我告诉你一件事。

547
00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:07.000
If Mom Detectives ever happens.
如果《妈妈侦探》真的开拍了。

548
00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:07.920
There we go.
那就这么定了。

549
00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:08.600
You're our director.
你就是我们的导演。

550
00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:09.460
Okay, very good.
好的，太棒了。

551
00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:10.740
Yes, for sure.
没错，肯定的。

552
00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:11.300
Right?
对吧？

553
00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:12.000
That's right.
确实如此。

554
00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:13.160
We'd have so much fun.
我们会玩得很开心的。

555
00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:13.460
I would love that.
我很乐意。

556
00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:15.700
Well, we know he's good at shooting stakeouts.
好吧，我们知道他很擅长拍摄监视任务。

557
00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:17.460
And there are a lot of those in Mom Detectives.
而且《妈妈侦探》里有很多这种戏份。

558
00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:17.940
Exactly.
没错。

559
00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:18.620
Exactly.
正是如此。

560
00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:21.080
I've experienced picking binoculars and everything.
我体验过挑选望远镜之类的所有事情。

561
00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:24.540
Well, you did just confess you didn't pick the right ones.
好吧，你刚才确实承认你没选对。

562
00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:26.760
So we will take that into consideration.
所以我们会把这一点考虑进去的。

563
00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:27.400
Let's delete that.
删掉那段吧。

564
00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:29.860
We'll take that part out.
我们会把那部分剪掉。

565
00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:32.680
Aw, Lee, thank you for coming in.
噢，李，谢谢你过来。

566
00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:34.080
It was so fun to have you here.
你能来这里真是太有趣了。

567
00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:34.960
So fun, y'all.
太有趣了，伙计们。

568
00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:36.400
Thank you for having me.
谢谢你们邀请我。

569
00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:37.440
What a blaSt.
真是太棒了。

570
00:22:37.480 --> 00:22:39.180
It's so fun to sit in this little room with you guys.
能和你们坐在这个小房间里真是太有趣了。

571
00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:41.020
Thank you so much, Lee.
非常感谢你，李。

572
00:22:41.020 --> 00:22:41.700
I love you, buddy.
我爱你，伙计。

573
00:22:41.800 --> 00:22:42.680
I'm coming in for a hug.
我要过来抱一下。

574
00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:43.120
Aw, yeah.
噢，好啊。

575
00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:43.700
All right.
好的。

576
00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.560
Well, we'll take a break and we'll say goodbye to Lee.
好了，我们要休息一下，和李说再见了。

577
00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:47.720
I might give him a smooch on the way out the door.
我出门的时候可能会亲他一下。

578
00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:50.680
And then we'll be back to break down the rest of vandalism.
然后我们会回来继续解析剩下的关于破坏公物的内容。

579
00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:51.800
I'm going to eat him out of line.
我要把他吃干抹净。

580
00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:04.230
How fun was that?
刚才多有趣啊？

581
00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:08.350
I did linger in the parking lot.
我确实在停车场逗留了一会儿。

582
00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:09.750
You were gone for a bit.
你确实离开了一阵子。

583
00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:12.070
He's very handsome as well, everyone.
他长得也非常帅，各位。

584
00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:13.390
He's a cutie.
他是个可爱的人。

585
00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:14.230
He is.
确实是。

586
00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:18.610
And I just, it was like you get to bring your lover to work.
我只是觉得，这就像是你带爱人来上班一样。

587
00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:19.910
Oh, gosh.
噢，天哪。

588
00:23:20.050 --> 00:23:21.470
I don't know why I did it.
我不知道我为什么要那么做。

589
00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:22.510
Now you're Toby.
现在你变成托比了。

590
00:23:22.990 --> 00:23:23.230
Oh, no.
噢，不。

591
00:23:23.410 --> 00:23:24.070
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

592
00:23:24.370 --> 00:23:25.750
Oh, you Toby-ed us.
噢，你对我们使了托比那一套。

593
00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:28.230
Well, let's start this episode.
好了，让我们开始这一集吧。

594
00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:30.910
It's going to begin with a cold open.
节目将以冷开场开始。

595
00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:32.910
Nellie can't seem to find Daryl.
内莉似乎找不到达里尔了。

596
00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:34.290
And Aaron's like, you know what?
亚伦就说，你知道吗？

597
00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:35.730
He's around here somewhere.
他就在这附近某处。

598
00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.390
Just a regular Thursday.
只是一个普通的周四。

599
00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.010
Aaron is giddy.
亚伦很兴奋。

600
00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:41.470
She's acting kind of stranger than normal.
她表现得比平时更奇怪了。

601
00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:46.870
And we find out that in her mind, she's helping Daryl pull off his whole secret other job.
我们发现，在她看来，她是在帮达里尔完成他那份秘密的副业。

602
00:23:46.870 --> 00:23:48.870
Yes, it's their big sneaky sneak.
没错，这是他们的大型秘密行动。

603
00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:49.990
Sneaky sneaks.
秘密行动。

604
00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:55.570
Part of this ruse involves a giant bear named Baryl.
这个计谋的一部分涉及一只名叫巴里尔的巨型熊。

605
00:23:55.790 --> 00:23:58.330
It wears a shirt.
它还穿着一件衬衫。

606
00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:02.690
And she sets it in his chair in his office.
她把它放在了他办公室的椅子上。

607
00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:03.590
Yes.
是的。

608
00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:09.790
I want to point out that we did have a secret conversation in the place where all secret conversations happen.
我想指出的是，我们确实在所有秘密谈话发生的地方进行了一次秘密谈话。

609
00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:11.830
The super secret stairwell.
那个超级秘密楼梯间。

610
00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:12.730
That's right.
没错。

611
00:24:13.070 --> 00:24:15.710
The super secret stairwell for sneaky sneaks.
那个专供秘密行动使用的超级秘密楼梯间。

612
00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:16.550
There it is.
就是那里。

613
00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:16.990
Yeah.
是啊。

614
00:24:17.670 --> 00:24:19.530
We had a fan question from Lee M.
我们收到了来自圣何塞的李·M的一位粉丝提问，

615
00:24:19.610 --> 00:24:22.190
in San Jose who said,
他说，

616
00:24:22.270 --> 00:24:28.250
it looks like there's a piece of painter's tape on the back of Daryl's jacket in the scene in the stairwell.
在楼梯间的那场戏里，达里尔的夹克背面好像贴了一块美纹纸胶带。

617
00:24:28.470 --> 00:24:29.290
What is this?
这是什么？

618
00:24:29.930 --> 00:24:31.910
Lee M., I looked at it.
