然后当帕姆进来时，瓦尔本打算向她道歉并说：“我也是刚看到。”

772
00:31:22.200 --> 00:31:24.760
I think the guys got drunk last night and did it.
“我想是那帮家伙昨晚喝醉了干的。”

773
00:31:25.680 --> 00:31:26.120
Okay.
好的。

774
00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:27.700
So that was like the original moment.
所以那才是最初的设定。

775
00:31:27.700 --> 00:31:31.780
Then, in the original shooting draft, it was described like this.
后来，在最初的拍摄剧本中，它是这样描述的。

776
00:31:32.220 --> 00:31:32.820
Quote,
引用如下：

777
00:31:33.060 --> 00:31:36.760
The mural now has some obvious striking graffiti on it.
壁画上现在有一些显眼的涂鸦。

778
00:31:36.900 --> 00:31:41.900
There are a couple of crudely drawn butts, and someone has written this sucks.
上面画着几个粗糙的屁股，还有人写了“这烂透了”。

779
00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:44.560
And then they took out that extra part with Val.
然后他们删掉了瓦尔的那部分戏份。

780
00:31:44.940 --> 00:31:48.260
And, Bailey, standards and practices did have notes on this.
而且，Bailey，审查部门确实对此提出了意见。

781
00:31:48.780 --> 00:31:49.160
I bet.
我敢肯定。

782
00:31:49.460 --> 00:31:50.580
Here is what they said.
他们是这么说的。

783
00:31:50.740 --> 00:31:51.560
They said,
他们说：

784
00:31:52.040 --> 00:31:56.320
The crudely painted butts on the wall should not be lifelike in appearance.
墙上粗糙的屁股涂鸦外观不能太逼真。

785
00:31:58.980 --> 00:31:59.460
Lifelike.
逼真。

786
00:31:59.620 --> 00:31:59.780
Yes.
是的。

787
00:31:59.920 --> 00:32:00.980
Very cartoony.
要非常卡通化。

788
00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:02.300
Can't be too realistic.
不能太写实。

789
00:32:02.720 --> 00:32:03.000
Exactly.
没错。

790
00:32:03.900 --> 00:32:09.520
Well, you know, I asked our writer, Owen, was it always the plan for Pam's mural to be vandalized?
嗯，你知道，我问过我们的编剧欧文，帕姆的壁画被涂鸦一直都在计划之中吗？

791
00:32:09.680 --> 00:32:11.160
And here's what he had to say.
他是这么说的。

792
00:32:11.760 --> 00:32:13.980
He said he didn't think it was always the plan.
他说他觉得这并不一直在计划中。

793
00:32:14.380 --> 00:32:18.200
It started as a way for Pam to flex her art muscles at work.
最初只是为了让帕姆在工作中展示一下她的艺术才华。

794
00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:21.380
But then when they started the storyline with Brian the Boom Guy,
但后来当他们开始写布莱恩（收音师）的故事线时，

795
00:32:21.660 --> 00:32:26.620
they wanted to create an intense situation for Pam that he could help her with.
他们想为帕姆创造一个紧张的局面，好让他能帮上忙。

796
00:32:26.620 --> 00:32:29.560
So, the fight over the mural fit right in.
所以，关于壁画的争执就顺理成章地加进来了。

797
00:32:30.340 --> 00:32:30.580
Yes.
是的。

798
00:32:30.840 --> 00:32:31.660
You know, and it's interesting.
你知道，这很有趣。

799
00:32:31.680 --> 00:32:36.460
I remember being in these discussions because, you know, a big question when we decided on
我记得当时参与了这些讨论，因为你知道，当我们决定这条故事线时，一个大问题就是，

800
00:32:36.460 --> 00:32:38.440
this storyline was, well, who did it?
到底是谁干的？

801
00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:39.020
Right.
没错。

802
00:32:39.180 --> 00:32:40.900
Because whoever did it is going to get fired.
因为不管是谁干的，都会被解雇。

803
00:32:41.540 --> 00:32:48.400
And we kind of thought, like, oh, Hide had been giving Pam grief when she was painting.
我们当时就在想，噢，海德在帕姆画画的时候一直找她麻烦。

804
00:32:48.760 --> 00:32:49.540
Maybe it's him.
也许是他干的。

805
00:32:49.840 --> 00:32:55.100
Wait, can I say in defense of Hide, not so much grief as just, like, hey, get started.
等等，我得为海德辩解一下，与其说是找麻烦，不如说是，嘿，赶紧开始吧。

806
00:32:55.100 --> 00:32:56.580
He had, like, had critiques.
他当时，就是提了一些批评意见。

807
00:32:56.740 --> 00:32:57.520
He had thoughts.
他有一些想法。

808
00:32:57.520 --> 00:33:00.780
But it wasn't so much like he was not a fan of what she was doing.
但并不是说他不喜欢帕姆画的东西。

809
00:33:00.780 --> 00:33:03.080
He just had a lot of opinions about it.
他只是对那幅画有很多看法而已。

810
00:33:03.300 --> 00:33:03.500
Yes.
是的。

811
00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:05.260
But we didn't want to fire Hide.
但我们不想解雇海德。

812
00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:06.260
Of course not.
当然不想。

813
00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:11.720
So, we did that kind of sneaky sneak thing where we're like, I guess we'll reveal a new
所以，我们耍了个小聪明，就像是说，我想我们得引入一个新角色，

814
00:33:11.720 --> 00:33:14.540
warehouse worker who will be responsible for this.
一个要为这件事负责的仓库员工。

815
00:33:14.660 --> 00:33:16.500
That's how they came up with the character of Frank.
这就是他们想出弗兰克这个角色的过程。

816
00:33:16.680 --> 00:33:22.280
But another thing was that later we knew that Frank and Brian were going to fight it out.
但还有一点是，我们后来知道弗兰克和布莱恩要打一架。

817
00:33:22.280 --> 00:33:22.700
Yeah.
没错。

818
00:33:23.060 --> 00:33:28.120
And, you know, Brian the boom guy was, like, a kind of big, muscly guy.
而且，你知道，收音师布莱恩是个大块头，肌肉发达。

819
00:33:28.700 --> 00:33:31.060
And we didn't want him to beat up Hide.
我们不想让他揍海德。

820
00:33:31.360 --> 00:33:34.660
That didn't seem – also, Hide didn't seem like a person who would, like, throw punches
这看起来不太对劲——而且，海德看起来也不像是那种会为了这件事

821
00:33:34.660 --> 00:33:35.440
over this, right?
挥拳相向的人，对吧？

822
00:33:35.440 --> 00:33:37.120
No, Hide's not going to charge Pam.
没错，海德不会去冲撞帕姆的。

823
00:33:37.280 --> 00:33:37.480
No.
不会。

824
00:33:37.600 --> 00:33:39.040
I think Hide actually likes Pam.
我觉得海德其实挺喜欢帕姆的。

825
00:33:39.200 --> 00:33:41.660
He just has opinions about her art, like I said.
就像我说的，他只是对她的艺术有看法而已。

826
00:33:41.840 --> 00:33:47.740
But I totally see in casting that you needed someone big who looked intimidating if they
但我完全明白在选角时，你需要一个看起来高大威猛、

827
00:33:47.740 --> 00:33:48.540
were going to run at you.
冲过来时很有震慑力的人。

828
00:33:48.780 --> 00:33:49.180
Exactly.
没错。

829
00:33:49.600 --> 00:33:50.640
I mean, we'll get to it.
我是说，我们之后会聊到这个。

830
00:33:50.720 --> 00:33:51.800
We're a little ahead of ourselves.
我们有点超前了。

831
00:33:51.800 --> 00:33:52.780
Yeah, we'll get to it.
是的，我们之后会聊到。

832
00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:56.800
But this is everything that went into, like, the discussion of this storyline.
但这就是关于这个故事情节讨论的所有背景。

833
00:33:57.080 --> 00:33:57.280
Right.
没错。

834
00:33:57.820 --> 00:34:00.520
Speaking of Hide, I have the cutest thing to share with you.
说到海德，我有一件超级可爱的事要跟你分享。

835
00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:01.300
What is it?
什么事？

836
00:34:01.420 --> 00:34:05.240
So, you know, we just had that eclipse, right?
你知道，我们刚经历了那次日食，对吧？

837
00:34:05.440 --> 00:34:05.640
Yeah.
是的。

838
00:34:05.880 --> 00:34:11.080
And I was talking about it in my Insta stories about the path of totality and all of that
我在我的Instagram快拍里谈到了它，提到了全食带之类的，

839
00:34:11.080 --> 00:34:13.480
because I love that title.
因为我太喜欢这个标题了。

840
00:34:13.660 --> 00:34:15.960
Like, and they said it so many times, the path of totality.
就像，他们说了好多次“全食带”。

841
00:34:16.220 --> 00:34:17.380
Are you in the path of totality?
你在全食带里吗？

842
00:34:17.500 --> 00:34:18.720
I was like, this should be a movie.
我就想，这应该拍成电影。

843
00:34:18.960 --> 00:34:19.320
Right?
对吧？

844
00:34:19.320 --> 00:34:19.540
Right?
对吧？

845
00:34:19.700 --> 00:34:22.240
This should be a rom-com called The Path of Totality.
这应该是一部叫《全食带》的浪漫喜剧。

846
00:34:22.480 --> 00:34:25.180
But anyway, I was going on and on about it.
总之，我当时一直在念叨这个。

847
00:34:25.320 --> 00:34:28.460
And then a few people sent me pictures they took of the eclipse.
然后有几个人给我发了他们拍的日食照片。

848
00:34:28.660 --> 00:34:31.860
And Hide sent me a video that he took of the eclipse.
海德给我发了一段他拍的日食视频。

849
00:34:32.020 --> 00:34:32.200
What?
真的吗？

850
00:34:32.480 --> 00:34:32.700
Yeah.
是的。

851
00:34:32.920 --> 00:34:34.520
And I was like, Hide, this is amazing.
我当时就说，海德，这太棒了。

852
00:34:34.540 --> 00:34:35.660
And he was like, thank you.
他说，谢谢你。

853
00:34:36.080 --> 00:34:38.440
Yeah, but he wasn't in the path of totality, right?
是啊，但他当时不在全食带里，对吧？

854
00:34:38.620 --> 00:34:39.500
It was a partial.
那是偏食。

855
00:34:39.740 --> 00:34:40.620
He was in the partial.
他是在偏食带里。

856
00:34:40.860 --> 00:34:42.360
Here in California, we got partial.
我们在加州这边看到的是偏食。

857
00:34:42.360 --> 00:34:44.180
But he still sent me his video of it.
但他还是把视频发给我了。

858
00:34:44.360 --> 00:34:45.280
Look, here it is.
你看，就是这个。

859
00:34:46.980 --> 00:34:48.080
Oh, it's really good.
噢，拍得真好。

860
00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:49.000
It's cool, isn't it?
很酷，对吧？

861
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:50.680
I don't even understand how he got that.
我甚至不知道他是怎么拍到的。

862
00:34:51.140 --> 00:34:51.660
All right.
好吧。

863
00:34:51.740 --> 00:34:56.000
Well, next up, Angela enters simply to announce that she'll be leaving.
那么，接下来，安吉拉进来只是为了宣布她要走了。

864
00:34:56.320 --> 00:34:56.720
Yes.
是的。

865
00:34:56.840 --> 00:34:59.120
Basically, you've come to work to tell us you're leaving early.
基本上，你来上班就是为了告诉我们你要早退。

866
00:34:59.300 --> 00:35:00.140
You're so proud.
你真骄傲。

867
00:35:00.340 --> 00:35:01.100
I'm so proud.
我真骄傲。

868
00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:02.180
I'm so dressed up.
我打扮得真漂亮。

869
00:35:02.320 --> 00:35:04.000
I'm ready for a very fancy day.
我准备好迎接非常时髦的一天了。

870
00:35:04.400 --> 00:35:08.460
Real quick, at 1 minute 53 seconds, we have a new Meredith wig.
快速说一下，在1分53秒处，梅雷迪思换了顶新假发。

871
00:35:08.960 --> 00:35:12.020
It is a dirty blonde, I would say a mullet.
那是深金色的，我觉得是鲻鱼头。

872
00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:13.400
I think this is a mullet.
我觉得这就是鲻鱼头。

873
00:35:13.540 --> 00:35:15.020
It is mullet-like, yes.
确实很像鲻鱼头，没错。

874
00:35:15.660 --> 00:35:16.020
Yes.
是的。

875
00:35:16.620 --> 00:35:20.320
Angela is going to go on to tell everyone that it's Phillip's first birthday,
安吉拉接下来要告诉大家今天是菲利普的一岁生日，

876
00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:22.440
and they're hosting a party at their house.
他们要在家里举办派对。

877
00:35:22.900 --> 00:35:25.500
Aaron says, oh, cute, so there'll be a bunch of kids.
亚伦说，噢，真可爱，那会有很多孩子吧。

878
00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:28.220
And Angela says, oh, no, no children.
安吉拉说，噢，不，没有孩子。

879
00:35:28.440 --> 00:35:29.940
Our house is not kid-friendly.
我们家不适合孩子。

880
00:35:30.340 --> 00:35:31.940
Most of our furniture is sharp.
我们大部分家具都有尖角。

881
00:35:32.140 --> 00:35:34.760
Also, ew, it will be mostly campaign donors.
而且，咦，来的大部分都是竞选捐款人。

882
00:35:35.660 --> 00:35:36.060
Ange?
安吉？

883
00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:36.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

884
00:35:37.180 --> 00:35:39.200
We got a lot of fan mail about your hair.
我们收到了很多关于你发型的粉丝来信。

885
00:35:39.480 --> 00:35:40.220
Oh, really?
噢，真的吗？

886
00:35:40.820 --> 00:35:42.300
Particularly from Hannah H.
特别是来自俄亥俄州克利夫兰的汉娜·H，

887
00:35:42.380 --> 00:35:43.980
in Cleveland, Ohio, who said,
她说，

888
00:35:44.260 --> 00:35:47.920
Angela, your hair is drop-dead gorgeous in this episode.
安吉拉，你这一集的发型美得惊人。

889
00:35:47.980 --> 00:35:48.420
Hannah!
汉娜！

890
00:35:48.900 --> 00:35:51.900
Would love to hear how this hairstyle was decided upon.
很想知道这个发型是怎么定下来的。

891
00:35:52.100 --> 00:35:53.940
Oh, my gosh, Hannah, you just made my day.
天哪，汉娜，你让我今天太开心了。

892
00:35:54.280 --> 00:35:55.500
Drop-dead gorgeous.
美得惊人。

893
00:35:55.940 --> 00:35:58.000
You know, this was so fun for Kim and I.
你知道，这对我跟金来说太有趣了。

894
00:35:58.180 --> 00:35:59.960
Kim Ferry, who did my hair on the show,
金·费里，她在剧中负责我的发型，

895
00:36:00.440 --> 00:36:02.760
we knew we wanted a half-up, half-down,
我们当时就知道想要半扎半披的发型，

896
00:36:02.940 --> 00:36:05.160
but she wanted to do something fancy.
但她想弄点花样。

897
00:36:05.160 --> 00:36:06.800
See, Kim is phenomenal with hair.
你看，金在发型设计上简直神了。

898
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:10.180
And so she was like, what about a little swirly thing in the back,
所以她说，要在后面弄个小卷，

899
00:36:10.280 --> 00:36:11.160
and then we'll flip it up.
然后再把它翻上去。

900
00:36:11.340 --> 00:36:12.760
This was all Kim's vision.
这全是金的构思。

901
00:36:12.940 --> 00:36:14.440
She had a total vision for it.
她对这个造型有完整的构想。

902
00:36:14.580 --> 00:36:16.560
I said, just go for it, Kim.
我说，尽管去做吧，金。

903
00:36:16.560 --> 00:36:17.260
I'm here.
我在这儿呢。

904
00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:18.360
I am your canvas.
我就是你的画布。

905
00:36:19.020 --> 00:36:21.000
And then I got to go have a costume fitting,
然后我去试了装，

906
00:36:21.160 --> 00:36:22.320
and they paired it with this dress,
他们给配了这件裙子，

907
00:36:22.400 --> 00:36:23.440
and it just all came together.
一切就都完美契合了。

908
00:36:23.980 --> 00:36:25.980
You know, I always felt bad for Kim Ferry,
你知道，我一直为金·费里感到难过，

909
00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:28.340
because she was forced to do this just
因为她被迫只能给我们所有人做这种

910
00:36:29.180 --> 00:36:33.060
kind of boring, everyday hair on all of us.
平淡无奇的日常发型。

911
00:36:33.140 --> 00:36:33.600
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

912
00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:34.440
All the time.
一直都是。

913
00:36:34.640 --> 00:36:36.120
Nothing ever fancy.
从没弄过什么花哨的。

914
00:36:36.400 --> 00:36:37.680
And so when it came along.
所以当这个机会来临时。

915
00:36:37.860 --> 00:36:38.640
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

916
00:36:38.720 --> 00:36:42.660
And because also, she is so good at the fancy hair.
而且因为她其实非常擅长做那种精致的发型。

917
00:36:42.840 --> 00:36:43.080
Yeah.
没错。

918
00:36:43.240 --> 00:36:44.860
She is so good at an updo.
她特别擅长盘发。

919
00:36:45.140 --> 00:36:46.640
She is so good at event hair.
她特别擅长做活动造型。

920
00:36:46.940 --> 00:36:47.340
Yes.
是的。

921
00:36:47.340 --> 00:36:50.360
Like, if you need someone to zhuzh you for your wedding,
比如，如果你婚礼需要人帮你打理造型，

922
00:36:50.580 --> 00:36:51.260
she's your gal.
找她准没错。

923
00:36:51.260 --> 00:36:52.460
Or a red carpet.
或者走红毯的时候。

924
00:36:52.720 --> 00:36:56.760
Like, oh, so for her to just have to do low ponies every week.
所以，她每周只能做低马尾真是太委屈她了。

925
00:36:56.940 --> 00:36:57.600
I know.
我懂。

926
00:36:57.720 --> 00:36:58.800
Or just a flat iron.
或者只是用直板夹拉直。

927
00:36:58.980 --> 00:36:59.420
Exactly.
确实。

928
00:36:59.780 --> 00:37:00.300
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

929
00:37:00.440 --> 00:37:01.720
That was a lot of fun, Hannah.
那真的很有趣，汉娜。

930
00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:02.340
Thank you.
谢谢你。

931
00:37:02.640 --> 00:37:03.660
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

932
00:37:04.020 --> 00:37:05.580
Oscar has a talking head,
奥斯卡有个单人访谈环节，

933
00:37:05.600 --> 00:37:09.360
and he's going to reveal that he will be attending this party.
他要透露他会参加这个派对。

934
00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:10.580
Yeah.
是啊。

935
00:37:11.400 --> 00:37:14.200
Oscar says, Angela's husband and I are in love.
奥斯卡说，安吉拉的丈夫和我相爱了。

936
00:37:14.320 --> 00:37:15.920
But as a politician in this town,
但作为这个镇上的政客，

937
00:37:16.020 --> 00:37:18.980
you still need the conventional blonde wife on your lawn signs.
你还是需要在竞选标语牌上放个传统的金发妻子。

