00:43:17.980 --> 00:43:21.720
It's clearly labeled with a piece of tape that says Daryl.
上面明明贴着一张写有“达里尔”的胶带。

1104
00:43:22.080 --> 00:43:22.640
Yeah.
没错。

1105
00:43:23.080 --> 00:43:24.300
And Daryl notices.
达里尔注意到了。

1106
00:43:24.700 --> 00:43:28.340
I think we should just skip ahead because I can't wait to talk about this.
我觉得我们应该直接跳到后面，因为我迫不及待想聊这个了。

1107
00:43:28.460 --> 00:43:29.200
Okay, let's do it.
好，那就这么办。

1108
00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:35.580
So the next beat in the storyline is that Daryl is going to call Jim out for taking his thermos.
剧情的下一个节奏是达里尔要当面指责吉姆拿了他的保温杯。

1109
00:43:35.760 --> 00:43:36.040
Yeah.
没错。

1110
00:43:36.040 --> 00:43:37.420
His clearly marked thermos.
那个标记明显的保温杯。

1111
00:43:37.520 --> 00:43:37.780
Yeah.
没错。

1112
00:43:37.780 --> 00:43:40.040
Yeah, I have an a-hole alert.
是啊，我警报响了，遇到混蛋了。

1113
00:43:43.320 --> 00:43:48.940
This begins a standoff in which Jim spitefully pours his coffee out into the trash can.
这引发了一场对峙，吉姆赌气地把咖啡倒进了垃圾桶里。

1114
00:43:49.080 --> 00:43:50.420
Daryl's like, man, you don't have to do that.
达里尔说，伙计，你没必要那样做。

1115
00:43:50.620 --> 00:43:55.420
But Jim just looks at him with this snarky look and pours it into the trash.
但吉姆只是带着那种刻薄的表情看着他，然后把咖啡倒进了垃圾桶。

1116
00:43:55.660 --> 00:43:59.260
And then he goes, do you want me to wash it out as well?
接着他说，要我顺便帮你洗了吗？

1117
00:43:59.260 --> 00:44:04.380
And Daryl says, oh, are you going to wash it or just let it soak?
达里尔说，哦，你是打算洗干净，还是就让它泡着？

1118
00:44:05.020 --> 00:44:06.700
Because now Daryl's had it.
因为达里尔现在忍无可忍了。

1119
00:44:07.060 --> 00:44:07.520
I know.
我知道。

1120
00:44:08.060 --> 00:44:10.900
Jim then just like hands him the thermos and he walks out.
吉姆随后就把保温杯递给他，然后走了出去。

1121
00:44:11.040 --> 00:44:17.600
But things would have further escalated with two back-to-back talking heads and they were in the shooting draft.
但事情本会进一步升级，剧本初稿里还有两段连续的采访镜头。

1122
00:44:17.800 --> 00:44:19.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1123
00:44:19.340 --> 00:44:20.420
Please share.
快分享一下。

1124
00:44:20.720 --> 00:44:22.780
It would have started with a Jim talking head.
首先会是吉姆的采访。

1125
00:44:23.140 --> 00:44:25.220
Jim says, Daryl's being weird.
吉姆说，达里尔怪怪的。

1126
00:44:25.220 --> 00:44:26.640
Roommates share stuff.
室友之间分享东西很正常。

1127
00:44:26.640 --> 00:44:27.760
It's not a big deal.
这没什么大不了的。

1128
00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:33.820
I mean, he can use my groceries when I buy some, which I'm gonna.
我是说，等我买了杂货他可以用我的，我正打算去买。

1129
00:44:34.240 --> 00:44:34.680
Okay.
好吧。

1130
00:44:35.100 --> 00:44:36.360
Then it would go to Daryl.
然后会切到达里尔。

1131
00:44:36.680 --> 00:44:38.840
Daryl would say, messy's one thing.
达里尔会说，邋遢是一回事。

1132
00:44:38.960 --> 00:44:40.440
Now he's screwing with my stuff.
现在他开始动我的东西了。

1133
00:44:40.600 --> 00:44:41.820
He holds up the thermos.
他举起保温杯。

1134
00:44:41.980 --> 00:44:42.720
You see that?
看到那个了吗？

1135
00:44:42.880 --> 00:44:43.840
That's peanut butter.
那是花生酱。

1136
00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:46.220
He got peanut butter on my thermos.
他在我的保温杯上弄了花生酱。

1137
00:44:46.400 --> 00:44:47.320
He shakes his head.
他摇了摇头。

1138
00:44:47.500 --> 00:44:48.620
You don't do that.
你不能那样做。

1139
00:44:48.620 --> 00:44:50.680
You don't go and do that.
你不能那样做。

1140
00:44:51.280 --> 00:44:54.920
Well, Jim's position is like, it's no big deal.
嗯，吉姆的立场是，这没什么大不了的。

1141
00:44:54.920 --> 00:44:55.340
Really?
真的吗？

1142
00:44:55.580 --> 00:44:57.460
You're gonna make a big deal out of this?
你要为了这个小题大做吗？

1143
00:44:57.620 --> 00:44:58.680
I'm using your thermos.
我只是用了你的保温杯。

1144
00:44:59.360 --> 00:45:02.580
So I have to ask the question, is it a big deal?
所以我得问个问题，这真的是小题大做吗？

1145
00:45:02.840 --> 00:45:04.460
If you and I were roommates.
如果我们俩是室友。

1146
00:45:04.700 --> 00:45:04.880
Yep.
没错。

1147
00:45:05.040 --> 00:45:14.180
And you had a thermos that you liked so much that you took a piece of tape and taped your name to it, I wouldn't use it.
如果你有一个非常喜欢的保温杯，甚至专门贴了胶带写上名字，我是不会去用的。

1148
00:45:14.180 --> 00:45:17.620
But I'd be like, clearly, this thermos means a lot to this person.
我会想，显然这个保温杯对这个人意义重大。

1149
00:45:17.880 --> 00:45:20.460
They have gone out of their way to label it.
他们特意给它做了标记。

1150
00:45:20.700 --> 00:45:21.700
I wouldn't use it.
我是不会去用的。

1151
00:45:21.960 --> 00:45:26.040
But isn't the point that, like, Daryl has labeled everything?
但重点难道不是，达里尔把所有东西都贴了标签吗？

1152
00:45:26.400 --> 00:45:29.080
Daryl doesn't really want to share anything, right?
达里尔其实什么都不想分享，对吧？

1153
00:45:29.400 --> 00:45:29.660
Hmm.
嗯。

1154
00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:31.360
Well, then that's your roommate.
好吧，那毕竟是你的室友。

1155
00:45:31.360 --> 00:45:31.960
Is he too fussy?
他太挑剔了吗？

1156
00:45:32.680 --> 00:45:34.160
Maybe, but that's your roommate.
也许吧，但那是你的室友。

1157
00:45:34.540 --> 00:45:41.120
But also, isn't he being forced into some of this fussiness in reaction to Jim's messiness?
但话说回来，他表现得这么挑剔，难道不是因为吉姆太邋遢，逼得他不得不这样吗？

1158
00:45:41.980 --> 00:45:47.020
Like, if he doesn't label his thermos and Jim uses it and doesn't wash it, then he doesn't have a thermos.
比如，如果他不给自己的保温杯贴标签，吉姆用了又不洗，那他就没杯子用了。

1159
00:45:47.200 --> 00:45:47.580
Exactly.
没错。

1160
00:45:47.580 --> 00:45:49.280
I support Daryl in this.
我支持达里尔的做法。

1161
00:45:49.420 --> 00:45:50.180
I support Daryl.
我支持达里尔。

1162
00:45:50.460 --> 00:45:53.080
Well, I think on that note, why don't we take a break?
好吧，既然说到这儿，我们不如休息一下？

1163
00:45:53.520 --> 00:45:53.960
Yes.
好。

1164
00:45:54.080 --> 00:45:58.060
And when we come back, Pam is hot to trot in the conference room.
等我们回来，帕姆就要在会议室大显身手了。

1165
00:46:09.940 --> 00:46:16.280
Let's head back to the Dunder Mifflin bullpen because Pam is just gonna burst into the office and say, conference room meeting.
让我们回到邓德·米夫林的办公区，因为帕姆马上要冲进办公室说：开会了，会议室集合。

1166
00:46:17.140 --> 00:46:18.520
I had so much fun doing that.
我刚才演得太开心了。

1167
00:46:18.520 --> 00:46:19.000
I bet.
我敢肯定。

1168
00:46:19.160 --> 00:46:19.640
I bet.
我敢肯定。

1169
00:46:19.840 --> 00:46:21.100
That's, like, the beSt.
那简直是最棒的。

1170
00:46:21.220 --> 00:46:23.180
That's, like, iconic office moment.
那简直是《办公室》里的经典时刻。

1171
00:46:23.820 --> 00:46:25.000
Everyone's like, what do you mean, Pam?
大家都在想，帕姆，你什么意思？

1172
00:46:25.380 --> 00:46:27.040
Why are you calling this conference room meeting?
你为什么要召集这个会议？

1173
00:46:27.140 --> 00:46:32.500
And she's like, listen, David Wallace gave me the clearance to do this.
然后她说，听着，是大卫·华莱士授权我这么做的。

1174
00:46:33.100 --> 00:46:34.200
And everyone's like, eh.
大家就，呃。

1175
00:46:34.300 --> 00:46:37.260
But then Dwight's like, conference room meeting and kind of gets Pam's back.
但接着德怀特说，会议室集合，算是支持了帕姆。

1176
00:46:37.380 --> 00:46:38.640
That's all he needed to hear.
他只需要听到这个就够了。

1177
00:46:38.840 --> 00:46:39.180
Yeah.
没错。

1178
00:46:39.420 --> 00:46:40.720
He's such a rule follower.
他真是个守规矩的人。

1179
00:46:41.640 --> 00:46:47.480
Well, everybody gathers in the conference room, and Pam is gonna explain that her mural has been vandalized.
好吧，大家聚集在会议室，帕姆要解释她的壁画被破坏了。

1180
00:46:47.600 --> 00:46:49.900
They put paint all over her mural.
有人在她的壁画上涂满了油漆。

1181
00:46:50.340 --> 00:46:54.400
So now Erin is like, but wait, didn't you want paint all over your mural?
于是艾琳就问，等等，你不是想要在壁画上涂油漆吗？

1182
00:46:54.540 --> 00:46:56.320
And Pam's like, yeah, but not that paint.
帕姆说，是啊，但不是那种油漆。

1183
00:46:56.400 --> 00:46:57.480
She goes, so different paints.
她说，是不同的油漆。

1184
00:46:57.640 --> 00:46:58.940
So it's, like, very funny.
所以这真的很好笑。

1185
00:46:59.140 --> 00:47:02.020
But the dynamic is so classic office.
但这种互动模式太经典了。

1186
00:47:02.260 --> 00:47:10.000
If you're a big fan of the show, I feel like you had to see the parallels of whenever Michael Scott would hold a meeting and everyone would interject and get him off topic.
如果你是这部剧的铁粉，我觉得你一定能看出其中的相似之处，就像迈克尔·斯科特每次开会，大家都会插嘴把他带跑偏一样。

1187
00:47:10.860 --> 00:47:11.860
It's so fun.
太好玩了。

1188
00:47:12.080 --> 00:47:14.020
I love that Pam also had this moment.
我喜欢帕姆也有这样的时刻。

1189
00:47:14.320 --> 00:47:20.180
Well, Meredith is gonna throw out that she's also upset because someone wrote her number on the men's room wall, and they got the number wrong.
梅雷迪思会抱怨说她也很生气，因为有人把她的号码写在男厕所墙上，而且号码还写错了。

1190
00:47:21.400 --> 00:47:23.560
It's 6782, not 6783.
是6782，不是6783。

1191
00:47:24.280 --> 00:47:32.240
And then Creed has this great line, and it's one of the ones I was talking about, where you watch these episodes so many times and you discover new things.
然后克里德说了句绝妙的台词，就是我之前提到的那种，当你看了很多遍剧集后，总能发现新东西。

1192
00:47:32.380 --> 00:47:32.560
Yes.
没错。

1193
00:47:32.660 --> 00:47:34.020
This line made me laugh so hard.
这句台词让我笑得不行。

1194
00:47:34.120 --> 00:47:38.380
He just goes, 6783, also a good time, less mileage.
他直接说，6783，那也不错，里程数更少。

1195
00:47:38.980 --> 00:47:39.640
So good.
太棒了。

1196
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:40.200
Oh, good.
哦，太好了。

1197
00:47:40.640 --> 00:47:43.000
And then Oscar is so funny.
还有奥斯卡也特别逗。

1198
00:47:43.120 --> 00:47:46.320
Oscar's like, you know, I just don't think anything can be done.
奥斯卡说，你知道，我觉得这事儿没法解决。

1199
00:47:46.980 --> 00:47:47.180
Yeah.
没错。

1200
00:47:47.500 --> 00:47:51.920
And I also love when Phyllis says, David Wallace called this meeting.
我也很喜欢菲利斯说的那句，是大卫·华莱士召集的会议。

1201
00:47:52.100 --> 00:47:52.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1202
00:47:52.340 --> 00:47:53.900
And Pam's like, he sure did.
帕姆就说，他确实这么做了。

1203
00:47:54.280 --> 00:47:54.780
Yes.
没错。

1204
00:47:55.040 --> 00:47:56.380
Well, listen, it's clear.
听着，这很清楚。

1205
00:47:56.520 --> 00:47:59.660
David Wallace did not call this meeting, and nobody cares.
大卫·华莱士并没有召集这次会议，也没人在乎。

1206
00:48:00.040 --> 00:48:00.800
No one cares.
没人在乎。

1207
00:48:00.980 --> 00:48:03.880
And everyone leaves except for Dwight and Nellie.
于是大家都走了，只剩下德怀特和奈莉。

1208
00:48:04.520 --> 00:48:06.440
They say they will help her.
他们说会帮她。

1209
00:48:06.960 --> 00:48:07.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1210
00:48:07.360 --> 00:48:09.340
Pam has a talking head where she says, you know what?
帕姆有个访谈镜头，她说，你知道吗？

1211
00:48:09.420 --> 00:48:13.260
She wanted this, like, righteous mob, but instead she ended up with Dwight and Nellie.
她想要的是那种正义的暴民，结果却只招来了德怀特和奈莉。

1212
00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:18.460
They do both have mob mentality, though, and she's pretty sure that Dwight has a pitchfork
不过他们俩确实都有暴民心态，而且她很确定德怀特的车里

1213
00:48:18.460 --> 00:48:19.000
in his car.
就有干草叉。

1214
00:48:19.220 --> 00:48:22.280
And then Dwight pokes his head in and he's like, you need my pitchfork?
然后德怀特探进头来说，你需要我的干草叉吗？

1215
00:48:22.560 --> 00:48:23.980
And he, like, runs out.
接着他就跑出去了。

1216
00:48:23.980 --> 00:48:26.780
We had a fan question about this, Angela.
安吉拉，我们有个关于这集的粉丝提问。

1217
00:48:27.500 --> 00:48:28.320
Antoine S.
来自马里兰州的安托万·S。

1218
00:48:28.580 --> 00:48:32.140
from Maryland said, I really hope you both read this and discuss.
说，我真心希望你们俩能读读并讨论一下。

1219
00:48:33.180 --> 00:48:36.940
This episode has become hard for me to watch, along with Scott's tots.
这一集和《斯科特的托儿们》一样，让我很难看下去。

1220
00:48:37.240 --> 00:48:37.520
Wow.
哇。

1221
00:48:38.020 --> 00:48:40.980
The vandalism of Pam's work is just downright mean.
对帕姆作品的破坏行为简直太卑劣了。

1222
00:48:41.340 --> 00:48:45.600
I know that some of these warehouse guys are newer, but I still can't believe someone would
我知道仓库里有些人是新来的，但我还是无法相信竟然有人会

1223
00:48:45.600 --> 00:48:46.100
do that.
做出那种事。

1224
00:48:46.700 --> 00:48:48.800
Furthermore, Val really upset me.
此外，瓦尔的表现真的让我很心烦。

1225
00:48:49.300 --> 00:48:52.600
How, as the boss of the warehouse, does she not step in at all?
作为仓库主管，她怎么能一点都不干预呢？

1226
00:48:53.060 --> 00:48:55.900
And then what about certain office workers?
还有办公室里的某些人呢？

1227
00:48:56.100 --> 00:48:58.880
Like, how do they not seem to care about Pam's feelings?
他们怎么好像一点都不在乎帕姆的感受？

1228
00:48:59.100 --> 00:49:03.540
After all of these years of working together, weddings, baby showers, they are just so indifferent
一起工作了这么多年，经历了婚礼、迎婴派对，他们对这种情况却如此冷漠。

1229
00:49:03.540 --> 00:49:04.900
to this situation.
对此情况。

1230
00:49:05.220 --> 00:49:07.220
You know, Antoine, this is a really good question.
安托万，这确实是个很好的问题。

1231
00:49:07.260 --> 00:49:14.200
I personally liked the iteration that you shared with us, Jenna, where they did write that Val
珍娜，我个人很喜欢你分享的那个版本，就是瓦尔

1232
00:49:14.200 --> 00:49:16.980
comes out and is like, oh my gosh, I'm so sorry.
出来说，天哪，我太抱歉了。

1233
00:49:17.120 --> 00:49:19.600
I think a bunch of the guys got drunk last night in the warehouse.
我想昨晚仓库里有一群人喝醉了。

1234
00:49:20.080 --> 00:49:22.320
That's the one that makes the most sense to me.
那个版本对我来说最合理。

1235
00:49:22.600 --> 00:49:22.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1236
00:49:22.880 --> 00:49:24.060
And they did write that.
他们确实写过那个版本。

1237
00:49:24.240 --> 00:49:29.440
I don't know how it didn't ultimately make it into the shooting draft, but I think there
我不知道为什么最终没能进入拍摄剧本，但我认为当时有一种感觉，

1238
00:49:29.440 --> 00:49:34.020
was this feeling that it wasn't as serious as it ended up being.
觉得这件事没最后呈现出来的那么严重。

1239
00:49:34.800 --> 00:49:35.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1240
00:49:35.220 --> 00:49:41.240
I have to say, I think this might be one of those times when like, they wrote this stuff
我不得不说，我觉得这可能就是那种情况，他们写了关于

1241
00:49:41.240 --> 00:49:47.540
about Val and then they took it out, but we all thought it had been addressed because
瓦尔的内容，后来又删掉了，但我们都以为问题已经解决了，因为

1242
00:49:47.540 --> 00:49:48.720
we knew about it.
我们知道有那段戏。

1243
00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:49.720
Does that make sense?
这说得通吗？

1244
00:49:49.720 --> 00:49:54.560
Yeah, but in taking it out, it does make her seem like she's not trying to help.
说得通，但删掉之后，确实让她看起来像是不想帮忙。

1245
00:49:54.740 --> 00:49:59.700
But there is, you know, there was way more in the shooting draft where Pam goes to Val's
但你知道，拍摄剧本里其实还有更多内容，比如帕姆去了瓦尔的

1246
00:49:59.700 --> 00:50:01.840
office and they have a whole conversation about it.
办公室，她们就此事进行了一整段对话。

1247
00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:04.940
It was a lot more fleshed out and none of it made it.
内容丰富得多，但最后全都没用上。

1248
00:50:05.080 --> 00:50:05.580
I know.
我知道。

1249
00:50:05.580 --> 00:50:11.700
So that to me for Val as a character is a disservice that it didn't make it.
所以对我来说，这对瓦尔这个角色来说是一种伤害，因为那些戏没能保留。

1250
00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:13.240
