我们在办公室拍那场审讯戏时笑得好厉害。

1411
00:56:51.400 --> 00:56:56.640
I remember the first time that I, like, slammed my hand down and I said, who did it?
我记得第一次，我用力拍桌子，然后说，是谁干的？

1412
00:56:56.920 --> 00:56:57.920
We all laughed.
我们都笑了。

1413
00:56:58.040 --> 00:56:58.660
I don't know why.
我也不知道为什么。

1414
00:56:58.760 --> 00:57:01.700
Like, everything about it was just so…
就觉得，一切都太……

1415
00:57:01.700 --> 00:57:02.420
Over the top.
太夸张了。

1416
00:57:02.560 --> 00:57:03.000
Yes.
是的。

1417
00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:03.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1418
00:57:03.340 --> 00:57:04.200
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1419
00:57:04.360 --> 00:57:05.720
We just laughed so hard in that room.
我们在那个房间里笑得前仰后合。

1420
00:57:05.920 --> 00:57:06.720
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

1421
00:57:06.860 --> 00:57:07.480
Frank did it.
是弗兰克干的。

1422
00:57:07.540 --> 00:57:07.840
Did it.
做到了。

1423
00:57:08.060 --> 00:57:08.780
I know.
我知道。

1424
00:57:09.180 --> 00:57:10.220
It's too good.
太精彩了。

1425
00:57:10.900 --> 00:57:14.340
Well, now we're going to go to the Lipton's party.
好了，现在我们要去立顿的派对了。

1426
00:57:14.820 --> 00:57:15.120
Yes.
好。

1427
00:57:15.600 --> 00:57:16.460
Kevin has come.
凯文也来了。

1428
00:57:17.260 --> 00:57:17.700
Yes.
是的。

1429
00:57:17.880 --> 00:57:19.140
Oh, we should say that.
噢，我们应该提一下那个。

1430
00:57:19.260 --> 00:57:22.040
When Dwight wasn't able to go, Kevin was like, I'll go.
当德怀特去不了的时候，凯文就说，我去。

1431
00:57:22.260 --> 00:57:23.500
And Angela's like, no.
安吉拉就说，不行。

1432
00:57:23.600 --> 00:57:26.300
And he goes, you're going to leave me here alone with all the money?
然后他说，你要把我一个人留在这里看着所有的钱吗？

1433
00:57:26.460 --> 00:57:27.360
And she's like, fine.
她就说，好吧。

1434
00:57:28.340 --> 00:57:31.200
Kevin is there for the appetizers.
凯文去那是为了开胃菜。

1435
00:57:31.680 --> 00:57:33.400
He's loving the puff pastries.
他超爱那些酥皮点心。

1436
00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:40.380
He and Oscar during the scene are standing below a ginormous portrait of Angela looking very stern.
那场戏里，他和奥斯卡站在一幅巨大的安吉拉画像下面，画像里的她看起来表情很严肃。

1437
00:57:40.760 --> 00:57:46.600
I would love for you guys to know that the set deck department gave me that ginormous painting of myself.
我想让你们知道，布景装饰部门把那幅巨大的画像送给了我。

1438
00:57:46.740 --> 00:57:48.520
It's like a print that looks like a painting.
那其实是一张看起来像油画的印刷品。

1439
00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:48.900
Yes.
没错。

1440
00:57:49.100 --> 00:57:49.760
In the frame.
还带了框。

1441
00:57:49.760 --> 00:57:50.680
I have it.
我留着呢。

1442
00:57:50.880 --> 00:57:52.280
For years, it hung in my hallway.
多年来，它一直挂在我的走廊里。

1443
00:57:52.740 --> 00:57:56.860
And then I thought, you know what?
后来我想，你知道吗？

1444
00:57:57.020 --> 00:57:58.160
That's just kind of weird.
这感觉有点怪怪的。

1445
00:57:58.340 --> 00:58:01.000
Like, when people come over and I took it down.
比如当有人来做客时，所以我把它取下来了。

1446
00:58:01.160 --> 00:58:02.400
I still have it, though.
不过我还是留着它。

1447
00:58:02.400 --> 00:58:03.600
Maybe I'll put it back up.
也许我该把它挂回去。

1448
00:58:04.140 --> 00:58:06.840
Matt Sohn was also DP, as Lee mentioned.
正如李提到的，马特·索恩也是摄影指导。

1449
00:58:07.020 --> 00:58:11.140
And he took a picture of me looking stern in front of a painting of myself looking stern.
他给我拍了一张照片，照片里的我表情严肃，站在一幅表情同样严肃的我的画像前。

1450
00:58:11.300 --> 00:58:12.160
And I have that picture.
那张照片我一直留着。

1451
00:58:12.320 --> 00:58:12.920
It's so great.
这太棒了。

1452
00:58:13.260 --> 00:58:15.140
That's what you need to blow up and put in your house.
那正是你需要放大并挂在家里展示的东西。

1453
00:58:15.280 --> 00:58:15.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1454
00:58:15.660 --> 00:58:16.600
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

1455
00:58:16.880 --> 00:58:23.000
You know, that's a funny quirk that I have seen sometimes when I go to entertainers' homes.
你知道吗，我去艺人家里时偶尔会看到这种有趣的怪癖。

1456
00:58:23.420 --> 00:58:29.920
There are kind of like the people that decorate their homes with giant portraits of themselves.
有些人喜欢用自己的巨幅肖像来装饰家里。

1457
00:58:30.700 --> 00:58:32.440
It's such a thing, right?
确实有这种事，对吧？

1458
00:58:32.880 --> 00:58:34.060
Do you know what I'm talking about?
你知道我在说什么吗？

1459
00:58:34.340 --> 00:58:34.520
Yeah.
知道。

1460
00:58:34.900 --> 00:58:35.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1461
00:58:35.300 --> 00:58:37.980
Some people have sort of like an ode to myself.
有些人就像是在为自己写赞美诗一样。

1462
00:58:38.440 --> 00:58:43.420
I would say in my home office, I have like the office memorabilia nook.
我得说，我的家庭办公室里有一个专门放工作纪念品的角落。

1463
00:58:44.980 --> 00:58:52.400
A lot of times I will get gifted giant portraits of myself throughout the years from a project,
很多时候，我会在项目结束后收到别人送我的巨幅个人肖像照，

1464
00:58:52.540 --> 00:58:53.880
kind of like what you're talking about.
就像你刚才说的那种。

1465
00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:54.180
Yeah.
没错。

1466
00:58:54.400 --> 00:58:56.760
But it'll even be like from a magazine shoot.
甚至连杂志拍摄的照片也会送来。

1467
00:58:56.960 --> 00:58:57.220
Yes.
是的。

1468
00:58:57.220 --> 00:59:05.440
And as like a thank you, they'll send to my house like a giant picture of my face or of me doing the shoot.
作为感谢，他们会寄给我一张我脸部的巨幅照片，或者是我拍摄时的照片。

1469
00:59:05.520 --> 00:59:08.500
And I always think to myself, what am I doing with this item?
我总是心想，我该拿这东西怎么办呢？

1470
00:59:08.760 --> 00:59:09.240
I know.
我懂。

1471
00:59:09.320 --> 00:59:12.420
I'm too shy to decorate my home with just portraits of me.
我太害羞了，没法用自己的肖像来装饰家里。

1472
00:59:12.480 --> 00:59:12.840
I know.
我明白。

1473
00:59:12.960 --> 00:59:13.440
It's weird.
这很奇怪。

1474
00:59:13.620 --> 00:59:14.180
It's really weird.
真的很奇怪。

1475
00:59:14.180 --> 00:59:17.160
I will say I have one picture of myself like that that's up.
不过我得说，我确实挂了一张那样的照片。

1476
00:59:17.260 --> 00:59:18.760
It is in my upstairs hallway.
它挂在楼上的走廊里。

1477
00:59:19.080 --> 00:59:21.120
So guests don't normally see it.
所以客人们通常看不到。

1478
00:59:21.160 --> 00:59:21.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1479
00:59:21.360 --> 00:59:28.160
But I did a photo shoot for an animal charity and I am dressed as Marie Antoinette and I'm holding
我曾为一个动物慈善机构拍过一组照片，我打扮成玛丽·安托瓦内特的样子，手里抱着

1480
00:59:28.160 --> 00:59:28.940
little kittens.
几只小猫。

1481
00:59:29.320 --> 00:59:30.420
I love that picture.
我超爱那张照片。

1482
00:59:30.680 --> 00:59:33.460
And the photographer, it was just this amazing photo.
摄影师拍得太棒了。

1483
00:59:33.820 --> 00:59:37.140
And after the shoot, they sent it to me in a giant frame.
拍摄结束后，他们把它装在一个巨大的相框里送给了我。

1484
00:59:37.720 --> 00:59:41.400
And it is above our piano in like our upstairs little alcove.
它现在挂在我们楼上小凹室的钢琴上方。

1485
00:59:41.560 --> 00:59:42.280
I love it.
我喜欢它。

1486
00:59:42.500 --> 00:59:43.280
I have one.
我也有一个。

1487
00:59:43.280 --> 00:59:44.200
So that's pretty cool.
那挺酷的。

1488
00:59:44.440 --> 00:59:45.320
That is kind of cool.
那确实还挺酷的。

1489
00:59:46.420 --> 00:59:49.860
One last thing, I did this project, which I can't talk about yet.
最后还有一件事，我做了一个项目，现在还不能透露。

1490
00:59:49.860 --> 00:59:52.560
And Zach Woods directed it.
是扎克·伍兹导演的。

1491
00:59:52.740 --> 00:59:53.540
I can't say that.
我不能说那个。

1492
00:59:53.940 --> 00:59:55.300
Zach Woods, amazing.
扎克·伍兹，太棒了。

1493
00:59:55.440 --> 00:59:55.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1494
00:59:55.700 --> 00:59:58.780
He directed it and he gave me a gift.
他执导了那个项目，还送了我一份礼物。

1495
00:59:59.140 --> 01:00:02.000
And it's a photo of myself doing this thing.
那是一张我做那件事时的照片。

1496
01:00:02.200 --> 01:00:03.920
At some point, I'm going to share it.
以后有机会我会分享出来的。

1497
01:00:04.040 --> 01:00:06.260
But I hung it in my podcast closet.
但我把它挂在我的播客录音间里了。

1498
01:00:06.540 --> 01:00:07.000
Okay.
好吧。

1499
01:00:07.340 --> 01:00:07.680
You know.
你懂的。

1500
01:00:07.760 --> 01:00:08.180
Very good.
非常好。

1501
01:00:08.500 --> 01:00:10.040
Not above your fireplace.
不能挂在你的壁炉上方。

1502
01:00:10.280 --> 01:00:12.200
Not above my fireplace or in my entryway.
不能挂在我的壁炉上方，也不能挂在我的玄关。

1503
01:00:12.640 --> 01:00:15.160
I do love the line that Oscar has here, though.
不过，我确实很喜欢奥斯卡在这里说的这句台词。

1504
01:00:15.160 --> 01:00:23.160
He sort of looks up at the painting and he made Brian break more than once because they
他抬头看了看那幅画，他让布莱恩笑场了好几次，因为他们

1505
01:00:23.160 --> 01:00:25.300
don't realize they're standing under the portrait.
没意识到自己正站在那幅肖像画下面。

1506
01:00:26.100 --> 01:00:28.040
And Oscar looks up at it.
然后奥斯卡抬头看了看它。

1507
01:00:28.140 --> 01:00:31.320
And there was one take where Oscar went, huh, like that.
有一条拍摄时，奥斯卡发出了“嗯”的一声。

1508
01:00:31.580 --> 01:00:33.740
And it made Brian crack up.
这让布莱恩笑喷了。

1509
01:00:33.880 --> 01:00:38.180
And he has this line where he says, how can anyone who weighs less than a guinea hen be
他还有句台词是这么说的：一个体重还没珍珠鸡重的人，怎么能

1510
01:00:38.180 --> 01:00:39.080
so terrifying?
这么吓人？

1511
01:00:40.960 --> 01:00:43.440
Well, now the senator and Angela come in.
好了，现在参议员和安吉拉进来了。

1512
01:00:43.560 --> 01:00:44.960
Angela, you're holding the baby.
安吉拉，你抱着孩子。

1513
01:00:45.160 --> 01:00:49.220
And we now know that this is the only take of this moment that was achieved.
我们现在知道，这是这一幕唯一拍成的一条。

1514
01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:51.520
Yes, we got this, I guess, in one take.
没错，我想我们一次就拍成了。

1515
01:00:51.760 --> 01:00:52.680
I didn't remember that.
我不记得了。

1516
01:00:52.780 --> 01:00:53.520
But oh, my gosh.
但是，天哪。

1517
01:00:53.940 --> 01:00:55.820
Here's how it read in the shooting draft.
这是剧本初稿里的内容。

1518
01:00:55.820 --> 01:00:57.720
I wanted to set the scene for you all.
我想为你们大家还原一下当时的场景。

1519
01:00:57.880 --> 01:01:01.040
The senator and Angela enter looking sharp.
参议员和安吉拉盛装登场。

1520
01:01:01.820 --> 01:01:05.500
Angela is holding Philip, who's dressed in a baptismal robe.
安吉拉抱着菲利普，他穿着洗礼袍。

1521
01:01:06.120 --> 01:01:10.720
Angela hands him to an Irish nurse, who immediately carries him back out of the room.
安吉拉把他交给了一位爱尔兰护士，护士立刻把他抱出了房间。

1522
01:01:11.800 --> 01:01:15.540
Senator Lipton would have said, thanks for coming, everyone.
利普顿参议员本该说：谢谢大家的光临。

1523
01:01:15.800 --> 01:01:17.520
Philip didn't realize he was so popular.
菲利普没想到自己这么受欢迎。

1524
01:01:18.500 --> 01:01:19.440
Everyone laughs.
大家都笑了。

1525
01:01:19.820 --> 01:01:22.180
Angela's laugh is especially hard.
安吉拉笑得特别大声。

1526
01:01:22.820 --> 01:01:25.880
I had a lot of fun doing that because I went, ha, ha, ha, ha.
我当时演得特别开心，因为我笑得是：哈哈哈哈。

1527
01:01:25.960 --> 01:01:26.760
I remember.
我记得。

1528
01:01:27.240 --> 01:01:28.580
Robert, you're terrible.
罗伯特，你真坏。

1529
01:01:28.860 --> 01:01:31.000
And then Angela notices a couple.
然后安吉拉注意到了一对夫妇。

1530
01:01:31.320 --> 01:01:34.040
Simon and Maxine, who let you guys in here?
西蒙和玛克辛，是谁让你们进来的？

1531
01:01:34.040 --> 01:01:35.720
More, more laughter.
又是一阵笑声。

1532
01:01:36.200 --> 01:01:37.840
Kevin, wow.
凯文，哇。

1533
01:01:38.200 --> 01:01:40.360
Turns out Angela and her husband are really funny.
原来安吉拉和她丈夫真的很幽默。

1534
01:01:41.100 --> 01:01:43.120
He finishes his hors d'oeuvre.
他吃完了开胃小菜。

1535
01:01:43.520 --> 01:01:44.660
Oscar looks sad.
奥斯卡看起来很伤心。

1536
01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:49.140
I loved it whenever my character got to take great pride in being the senator's wife.
我一直很喜欢我的角色为能成为参议员夫人而感到自豪的时刻。

1537
01:01:49.600 --> 01:01:52.340
Some of my favorite storyline beats.
那是我最喜欢的一些剧情点。

1538
01:01:52.560 --> 01:01:54.220
She loves being highfalutin.
她很享受那种高高在上的感觉。

1539
01:01:54.520 --> 01:01:55.520
This side of Angela.
安吉拉的这一面。

1540
01:01:55.680 --> 01:01:55.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1541
01:01:56.380 --> 01:01:58.820
We are now back in the conference room.
我们现在回到了会议室。

1542
01:01:59.040 --> 01:02:01.800
Nellie and Pam and Toby are all questioning Frank.
奈莉、帕姆和托比都在质问弗兰克。

1543
01:02:02.100 --> 01:02:03.160
Pam wants an apology.
帕姆想要一个道歉。

1544
01:02:04.180 --> 01:02:05.860
She wants him to fess up.
她想让他坦白。

1545
01:02:06.020 --> 01:02:06.560
That's right.
没错。

1546
01:02:06.800 --> 01:02:13.300
So I guess, Pam, to get his apology, her strategy is to first apologize to Frank if she did anything to upset him.
所以我想，帕姆为了得到他的道歉，她的策略是先向弗兰克道歉，如果她做了什么让他不高兴的事的话。

1547
01:02:13.460 --> 01:02:20.240
She's trying to be very diplomatic, but also it's, I think, it's a little bit patronizing, right?
她试图表现得非常圆滑，但我觉得，这也有点居高临下，对吧？

1548
01:02:20.400 --> 01:02:20.860
Well, yeah.
嗯，是啊。

1549
01:02:21.280 --> 01:02:22.860
Frank isn't having any of it.
弗兰克根本不吃这一套。

1550
01:02:23.020 --> 01:02:23.980
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1551
01:02:24.020 --> 01:02:26.840
I'll apologize for not liking your doodles.
我会为不喜欢你的涂鸦而道歉。

1552
01:02:27.840 --> 01:02:29.720
And he says that butts are funny.
他说屁股很好笑。

1553
01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:32.220
And he also says, and you know what?
他还说，你知道吗？

1554
01:02:32.400 --> 01:02:33.860
You can't fire me.
你不能解雇我。

1555
01:02:33.980 --> 01:02:35.120
And he leaves.
然后他就走了。

1556
01:02:35.660 --> 01:02:38.400
Toby was useless, basically, in this scene.
托比在这一幕里基本上毫无用处。

1557
01:02:38.640 --> 01:02:43.560
Now, you mentioned earlier that there was a storyline that got deleted.
你刚才提到有一个被删减的故事情节。

1558
01:02:43.560 --> 01:02:49.380
And I'm very curious about it, Angela, because I'm a little bit thinking, how did Toby get involved in this?
我对此很好奇，安吉拉，因为我在想，托比是怎么卷进来的？

1559
01:02:50.060 --> 01:02:50.200
Okay.
好的。

1560
01:02:50.400 --> 01:02:52.020
Well, he's the head of HR.
嗯，他是人力资源部主管。

1561
01:02:52.200 --> 01:02:52.460
Sure.
当然。

1562
01:02:52.640 --> 01:02:52.840
Right?
对吧？

1563
01:02:52.840 --> 01:02:56.620
And there was a deleted Toby runner that I loved.
有一个我非常喜欢的托比的删减片段。

1564
01:02:56.800 --> 01:02:57.960
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1565
01:02:58.180 --> 01:03:02.460
And basically, Toby is alone with Frank in the conference room.
基本上，托比和弗兰克单独在会议室里。

1566
01:03:02.640 --> 01:03:03.760
Pam and Nellie have left.
帕姆和奈莉已经离开了。

1567
01:03:03.900 --> 01:03:04.880
They have stepped outside.
她们走到了外面。

1568
01:03:05.000 --> 01:03:08.420
But they are watching through the glass, you know, window.
但她们透过玻璃窗在看着。

1569
01:03:08.860 --> 01:03:09.080
Yes.
是的。

1570
01:03:09.500 --> 01:03:11.660
And Toby is wanting to impress Nellie.
托比想给奈莉留下好印象。

1571
01:03:11.780 --> 01:03:14.600
So he's kind of under his breath as he's questioning Frank.
