凯文走进来对罗伯特说，谢谢你的食物，但你烂透了。

2207
01:29:31.060 --> 01:29:31.360
Yeah.
没错。

2208
01:29:31.500 --> 01:29:36.020
He said these two people care about you and you're just using them.
他说这两个人关心你，而你只是在利用他们。

2209
01:29:36.180 --> 01:29:37.760
But again, the food was great.
但话说回来，食物还是很棒的。

2210
01:29:38.400 --> 01:29:40.200
Oscar and Angela follow Kevin out.
奥斯卡和安吉拉跟着凯文走了出去。

2211
01:29:40.200 --> 01:29:43.600
Angela has a little smile on her face that Kevin stood up for her.
安吉拉脸上带着一丝微笑，因为凯文为她挺身而出。

2212
01:29:44.100 --> 01:29:47.720
There was this extended driving scene that Lee talked about.
李提到过一段很长的开车戏。

2213
01:29:47.960 --> 01:29:52.400
It starts with a Kevin talking head and then ends with the three of us in the car.
它以凯文的单人采访开始，最后是我们三个人在车里。

2214
01:29:52.460 --> 01:29:53.960
And I'd love for you guys to hear it.
我很想让你们听听这段。

2215
01:29:54.680 --> 01:29:58.940
I've sat next to Oscar and Angela for 14 years.
我和奥斯卡、安吉拉坐在一起14年了。

2216
01:29:59.200 --> 01:29:59.860
They're my people.
他们是我的伙伴。

2217
01:30:00.980 --> 01:30:06.980
If you just go by distance, they're my best friends.
如果只按距离算，他们是我最好的朋友。

2218
01:30:09.960 --> 01:30:12.440
I don't know why you go by distance, though, I guess.
不过我不知道为什么要按距离算，我想大概是吧。

2219
01:30:16.130 --> 01:30:18.330
Thanks for getting me all this stuff, Ange.
谢谢你帮我拿了这么多东西，安吉。

2220
01:30:19.010 --> 01:30:21.150
We had way too many appetizers anyway.
反正我们开胃菜点得太多了。

2221
01:30:21.670 --> 01:30:23.290
I don't know who did the ordering.
我不知道是谁点的餐。

2222
01:30:23.710 --> 01:30:25.510
How hard is it to buy for 40?
给40个人买东西有那么难吗？

2223
01:30:25.790 --> 01:30:27.430
Some people are just terrible at math.
有些人数学就是烂。

2224
01:30:27.610 --> 01:30:28.310
It's embarrassing.
真丢人。

2225
01:30:28.590 --> 01:30:28.810
It is.
确实。

2226
01:30:29.270 --> 01:30:29.630
Totally.
完全同意。

2227
01:30:31.070 --> 01:30:35.110
So they bond over this moment where people are bad at math.
所以他们因为人们数学不好这一点产生了共鸣。

2228
01:30:35.590 --> 01:30:37.850
I also love that Kevin's like, these are my people.
我也很喜欢凯文说“他们是我的伙伴”那段。

2229
01:30:38.150 --> 01:30:38.870
You know what?
你知道吗？

2230
01:30:38.950 --> 01:30:40.390
It's that thing that breaks my heart.
那正是让我心碎的地方。

2231
01:30:40.550 --> 01:30:44.830
That Brian Baumgartner does so well as Kevin when he gets that little quiver in his voice.
布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳在饰演凯文时，当他声音里带出那种颤抖时，表现得太好了。

2232
01:30:44.830 --> 01:30:45.250
Yeah.
没错。

2233
01:30:45.570 --> 01:30:46.710
And he gets like...
他变得……

2234
01:30:46.710 --> 01:30:47.290
Vulnerable.
脆弱。

2235
01:30:47.510 --> 01:30:48.030
Yes.
是的。

2236
01:30:48.690 --> 01:30:49.930
I'm so sweet.
我真是太贴心了。

2237
01:30:50.150 --> 01:30:50.930
Really sweet.
真的很贴心。

2238
01:30:50.930 --> 01:30:52.870
And that scene was so fun to do.
那场戏演起来真有趣。

2239
01:30:53.130 --> 01:30:56.570
Well, Owen Ellickson said that he loved that scene, Angela.
嗯，欧文·埃里克森说他很喜欢那场戏，安吉拉。

2240
01:30:56.810 --> 01:31:04.030
When we asked him, like, what were some of your favorite moments, he said, the three of you guys driving back from the party bonding over math mistakes.
当我们问他最喜欢的时刻有哪些时，他说，你们三个人从派对开车回来，因为数学错误而产生共鸣的那段。

2241
01:31:04.030 --> 01:31:09.690
He said, you guys played it beautifully, and I hope that scene makes the light of day at some point.
他说，你们演得太美妙了，希望那场戏有朝一日能重见天日。

2242
01:31:09.970 --> 01:31:11.270
Aw, thanks, Owen.
噢，谢谢你，欧文。

2243
01:31:11.530 --> 01:31:11.930
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2244
01:31:12.570 --> 01:31:14.910
Well, this scene is going to end with a tag.
好吧，这场戏将以一个片尾彩蛋结束。

2245
01:31:15.450 --> 01:31:17.650
Jim and Daryl's very clean apartment.
吉姆和达里尔非常整洁的公寓。

2246
01:31:18.170 --> 01:31:19.330
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

2247
01:31:19.490 --> 01:31:19.730
What?
怎么了？

2248
01:31:19.890 --> 01:31:22.230
It's actually not how the shooting draft ended.
那其实并不是拍摄剧本原本的结局。

2249
01:31:22.230 --> 01:31:28.490
So you describe how it ended when it aired, and I will share the final moment of the shooting draft.
所以你先描述一下播出时的结局，然后我来分享拍摄剧本的最终时刻。

2250
01:31:28.690 --> 01:31:28.930
Okay.
好的。

2251
01:31:29.570 --> 01:31:31.730
Well, Jim and Daryl are playing video games.
吉姆和达里尔正在玩电子游戏。

2252
01:31:31.890 --> 01:31:36.230
Daryl finishes the soda, and he crumples the can and throws it on the floor.
达里尔喝完了汽水，把罐子捏扁扔在了地板上。

2253
01:31:36.930 --> 01:31:38.930
And Jim says, how did that feel?
吉姆问，感觉怎么样？

2254
01:31:39.090 --> 01:31:39.870
Did it feel good?
感觉好吗？

2255
01:31:40.050 --> 01:31:41.770
And Daryl's like, it felt really good.
达里尔说，感觉真不错。

2256
01:31:41.990 --> 01:31:48.510
And then, if you want to know how John Krasinski laughs in real life, it is this laugh right here.
如果你想知道约翰·卡拉辛斯基现实生活中是怎么笑的，就是刚才那种笑法。

2257
01:31:48.510 --> 01:31:50.050
He got so tickled.
他被逗乐了。

2258
01:31:50.230 --> 01:31:51.390
That is pure J.K.
那才是纯粹的约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

2259
01:31:51.610 --> 01:31:51.870
Yep.
没错。

2260
01:31:53.370 --> 01:31:57.330
Well, this is how the episode ended in the shooting draft.
这就是拍摄剧本中这一集的结尾。

2261
01:31:57.810 --> 01:32:03.530
And, of course, once I read it to you, you'll understand why they decided not to end this way.
当然，我读给你听之后，你就会明白他们为什么决定不这样结尾了。

2262
01:32:03.690 --> 01:32:04.130
Okay.
好的。

2263
01:32:04.410 --> 01:32:07.590
Already with the uproar about Brian, the boom guy.
关于收音师布莱恩的骚动已经闹得沸沸扬扬了。

2264
01:32:07.790 --> 01:32:08.450
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

2265
01:32:08.490 --> 01:32:09.730
Is this something I've forgotten?
这是我忘记的事情吗？

2266
01:32:10.630 --> 01:32:15.310
Probably, but we did read it, and it was in the shooting draft, so that means they did shoot it.
可能吧，但我们确实读过，而且它在拍摄剧本里，这意味着他们确实拍了。

2267
01:32:15.630 --> 01:32:18.110
It would have ended with a Brian talking head.
结尾本来会是布莱恩的个人访谈。

2268
01:32:18.510 --> 01:32:19.690
After his scuffle.
在他打架之后。

2269
01:32:20.590 --> 01:32:20.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2270
01:32:21.590 --> 01:32:23.050
Brian talking head outside.
布莱恩在室外的个人访谈。

2271
01:32:23.510 --> 01:32:25.010
Brian's a little roughed up.
布莱恩看起来有点狼狈。

2272
01:32:25.590 --> 01:32:28.250
Brian says to the camera operator, fine.
布莱恩对摄影师说，行吧。

2273
01:32:28.650 --> 01:32:29.030
Okay.
好吧。

2274
01:32:29.390 --> 01:32:31.650
He turns to the documentarian and sighs.
他转向纪录片制作人，叹了口气。

2275
01:32:33.450 --> 01:32:34.710
I'm Brian Whittle.
我是布莱恩·惠特尔。

2276
01:32:35.130 --> 01:32:40.230
I was the boom mic operator on this documentary until about three minutes ago when they fired me.
我曾是这部纪录片的收音师，直到大约三分钟前他们解雇了我。

2277
01:32:40.710 --> 01:32:42.510
I don't regret stepping in.
我不后悔插手这件事。

2278
01:32:43.130 --> 01:32:44.750
Nobody messes with Pam.
没人能动帕姆。

2279
01:32:45.170 --> 01:32:46.290
Pam's my buddy.
帕姆是我的好朋友。

2280
01:32:46.290 --> 01:32:49.170
I spent nine years recording her voice.
我花了九年时间录制她的声音。

2281
01:32:49.370 --> 01:32:51.490
I followed her to art school in New York.
我甚至跟着她去了纽约的艺术学校。

2282
01:32:51.790 --> 01:32:55.860
Hell, if it wasn't for those no-interfere agreements we signed, I would have...
见鬼，要不是我们签了那些不得干预协议，我早就……

2283
01:32:56.770 --> 01:32:57.350
Whatever.
算了。

2284
01:32:57.970 --> 01:32:58.810
It's fine.
没关系。

2285
01:32:59.370 --> 01:33:00.930
Then he looks to the boom guy.
然后他看向收音师。

2286
01:33:01.730 --> 01:33:02.790
Hold it higher.
举高点。

2287
01:33:03.310 --> 01:33:04.350
Trust the mic.
相信麦克风。

2288
01:33:04.890 --> 01:33:05.730
Right there.
就在那儿。

2289
01:33:05.970 --> 01:33:06.430
See?
看到了吗？

2290
01:33:07.390 --> 01:33:07.970
Perfect.
完美。

2291
01:33:09.130 --> 01:33:10.050
Oh, no.
噢，不。

2292
01:33:10.430 --> 01:33:10.950
Yeah.
是啊。

2293
01:33:11.670 --> 01:33:13.370
That was in the shooting draft.
那是在拍摄剧本里的。

2294
01:33:13.610 --> 01:33:15.170
I think I remember that now.
我想我现在记起来了。

2295
01:33:15.470 --> 01:33:15.790
Yeah.
是啊。

2296
01:33:16.270 --> 01:33:19.950
If it wasn't for those don't-interfere agreements, I would have...
要不是那些不得干预协议，我早就……

2297
01:33:19.950 --> 01:33:20.630
Dot, dot, dot.
省略号。

2298
01:33:20.990 --> 01:33:21.290
Maybe.
也许吧。

2299
01:33:21.590 --> 01:33:21.950
Whatever.
算了。

2300
01:33:22.450 --> 01:33:23.190
You know what?
你知道吗？

2301
01:33:23.250 --> 01:33:25.090
That sounds like five dots to me.
听起来像是五个点。

2302
01:33:25.390 --> 01:33:27.630
Dot, dot, dot, dot, dot, dot.
点，点，点，点，点，点。

2303
01:33:27.950 --> 01:33:28.230
Yeah.
没错。

2304
01:33:28.710 --> 01:33:29.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2305
01:33:30.350 --> 01:33:31.970
Well, there you have it, everybody.
好了，大家都听到了。

2306
01:33:32.410 --> 01:33:34.070
That was vandalism.
那是蓄意破坏。

2307
01:33:34.330 --> 01:33:37.090
I think we have some big thank yous to shout out.
我想我们得大声感谢几位嘉宾。

2308
01:33:37.090 --> 01:33:42.770
Yes, a big thank you to my husband, Lee Kirk, for coming into the studio today and talking
是的，非常感谢我的丈夫李·柯克今天来到演播室和我们聊天。

2309
01:33:42.770 --> 01:33:43.370
with us.
和我们聊天。

2310
01:33:43.550 --> 01:33:49.230
Yes, and also to Owen Ellickson, our writer, who was so gracious in answering our fan questions.
是的，还要感谢我们的编剧欧文·埃利克森，他非常亲切地回答了粉丝们的问题。

2311
01:33:49.570 --> 01:33:52.470
Yes, Owen is currently working on St. Dennis Medical.
没错，欧文目前正在制作《圣丹尼斯医疗中心》。

2312
01:33:52.470 --> 01:33:58.330
It's an upcoming NBC comedy from The Office's own Justin Spitzer, but he'd also like to give
这是NBC即将推出的一部喜剧，由《办公室》的贾斯汀·斯皮策制作，但他还想特别提到

2313
01:33:58.330 --> 01:34:04.630
a shout out to Chocolate Milk, which he says is, quote, an excellent drink that deserves
巧克力牛奶，他说这是一种“绝佳的饮品，值得

2314
01:34:04.630 --> 01:34:07.310
more respect than adults give it, end quote.
成年人给予它更多的尊重”，引用结束。

2315
01:34:08.690 --> 01:34:09.650
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

2316
01:34:09.990 --> 01:34:14.610
And of course, a thank you to Steve Burgess and to all of you for your excellent questions
当然，还要感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯，以及感谢大家本周提出的精彩问题。

2317
01:34:14.610 --> 01:34:15.270
this week.
本周。

2318
01:34:15.430 --> 01:34:17.950
Yes, and to Josh for making us Madelines.
是的，还要感谢乔什为我们做了玛德琳蛋糕。

2319
01:34:18.310 --> 01:34:18.690
Yeah.
没错。

2320
01:34:19.070 --> 01:34:20.530
We had some good treats today.
我们今天吃到了很棒的零食。

2321
01:34:20.750 --> 01:34:24.890
We hope you guys have a great week, and we just love you and love doing this, and we'll
希望大家这周过得愉快，我们非常爱你们，也热爱做这个节目，我们下周见，

2322
01:34:24.890 --> 01:34:28.850
see you next week with an update on landlines.
届时会带来关于固定电话的最新消息。

2323
01:34:29.130 --> 01:34:29.830
See you then.
到时见。

2324
01:34:34.480 --> 01:34:36.420
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

2325
01:34:36.420 --> 01:34:40.860
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金赛制作。

2326
01:34:41.060 --> 01:34:43.360
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的高级制作人是卡西·杰金斯。

2327
01:34:43.560 --> 01:34:48.140
Our audio engineer is Jordan Duffy, and our associate producer is Ainsley Bubbaco.
我们的音频工程师是乔丹·达菲，助理制作人是安斯利·巴巴科。

2328
01:34:48.400 --> 01:34:51.340
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿创作的《橡胶树》。
